gging.\n\nThe main functionality added by this class over the built-in\nlogging.Logger class is the ability to keep track of the origin of the\nmessages, the ability to enable logging of warnings.warn calls and\nexceptions, and the addition of colorized output a", "start_line": 154, "end_line": 550}, {"name": "StreamHandler", "bases": ["logging.StreamHandler"], "methods": ["emit"], "docstring": "A specialized StreamHandler that logs INFO and DEBUG messages to\nstdout, and all other messages to stderr.  Also provides coloring\nof the output, if enabled in the parent logger.", "start_line": 553, "end_line": 585}, {"name": "FilterOrigin", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "filter"], "docstring": "A filter for the record origin.", "start_line": 588, "end_line": 595}, {"name": "ListHandler", "bases": ["logging.Handler"], "methods": ["__init__", "emit"], "docstring": "A handler that can be used to capture the records in a list.", "start_line": 598, "end_line": 606}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module defines a logging class based on the built-in logging module.\n\n.. note::\n\n    This module is meant for internal ``astropy`` usage. For use in other\n    packages, we recommend implementing your own logger instead.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "docs/wcs/examples/programmatic.py", "file_hash": "56ddfcf82c7380e47d96c92ebf0959f8cc7684c406db53c2e8dbed03315efcb3", "imports": [{"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["wcs"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.io", "names": ["fits"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "docs/wcs/examples/from_file.py", "file_hash": "1c1393c7a86432e1baa46897a71533657e0b72558fc29df4fbe7725d8c7b1d6a", "imports": [{"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astro