`val`` and ``val2``.  If neither is masked then the return ``mask``\nis ``None``.\n\nIf either ``val`` or ``val2`` are masked then they are replaced\nwith f", "start_line": 3207, "end_line": 3266, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_check_leapsec", "qualified_name": "_check_leapsec", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3279, "end_line": 3293, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_leap_seconds", "qualified_name": "update_leap_seconds", "args": ["files"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If the current ERFA leap second table is out of date, try to update it.\n\nUses `astropy.utils.iers.LeapSeconds.auto_open` to try to find an\nup-to-date table.  See that routine for the definition of \"out of date\".\n\nIn order to make it safe to call this any time, all exceptions are turned\ninto warnings", "start_line": 3296, "end_line": 3329, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_represent_as_dict_attrs", "qualified_name": "_represent_as_dict_attrs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 212, "end_line": 222, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "bound"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 224, "end_line": 240, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_sortable_arrays", "qualified_name": "get_sortable_arrays", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of arrays which can be lexically sorted to represent\nthe order of the parent column.\n\nReturns\n-------\narrays : list of ndarray", "start_line": 242, "end_line": 254, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 257, "end_line": 258, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_construct_from_dict", "qualified_name": "_construct_from_dict", "args": ["self", "map"], "decorators": [], "doc