"precision", "in_subfmt", "out_subfmt"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the internal _format, scale, and _time attrs from user\ninputs.  This handles coercion into the correct shapes and\nsome basic input validation.", "start_line": 486, "end_line": 553, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_time_fmt", "qualified_name": "_get_time_fmt", "args": ["self", "val", "val2", "format", "scale", "precision", "in_subfmt", "out_subfmt"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given the supplied val, val2, format and scale try to instantiate\nthe corresponding TimeFormat class to convert the input values into\nthe internal jd1 and jd2.\n\nIf format is `None` and the input is a string-type or object array then\nguess available formats and stop when one matches.", "start_line": 555, "end_line": 616, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "writeable", "qualified_name": "writeable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 619, "end_line": 620, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "writeable", "qualified_name": "writeable", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["writeable.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 623, "end_line": 625, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "format", "qualified_name": "format", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Get or set time format.\n\nThe format defines the way times are represented when accessed via the\n``.value`` attribute.  By default it is the same as the format used for\ninitializing the `Time` instance, but it can be set to any other value\nthat could be used for initialization.  These can be listed w", "start_line": 628, "end_line": 642, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "format", "qualified_name": "format", "args": ["self", "format"], "decorators": ["format.setter"], "docstring": "Set time format.", "start_line": 645, "end_line": 664, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_string", "qualified_name": "to_string", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Output a string representation of the Time or TimeDelta object.\n\nSimilar to ``str(self.value)`` (which uses numpy array formatting) but\narray values are evaluated only for the items that actually are output.\nFor large arrays this can be a substantial performance improvement.\n\nReturns\n-------\nout : s", "start_line": 666, "end_line": 691, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 693, "end_line": 696, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 698, "end_line": 699, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__hash__", "qualified_name": "__hash__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 701, "end_line": 717, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "scale", "qualified_name": "scale", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Time scale.", "start_line": 720, "end_line": 722, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_scale", "qualified_name": "_set_scale", "args": ["self", "scale"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This is the key routine that actually does time scale conversions.\nThis is not public and not connected to the read-only scale property.", "start_line": 724, "end_line": 787, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "precision", "qualified_name": "precision", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Decimal precision when outputting seconds as floating point (int\nvalue between 0 and 9 inclusive).", "start_line": 790, "end_line": 795, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "precision", "qualified_name": "precision", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": ["precision.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 798, "end_line": 800, "is_async": false, "is_metho