e value(s) in JD.", "start_line": 911, "end_line": 916, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "jd2", "qualified_name": "jd2", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Second of the two doubles that internally store time value(s) in JD.", "start_line": 919, "end_line": 924, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_value", "qualified_name": "to_value", "args": ["self", "format", "subfmt"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get time values expressed in specified output format.\n\nThis method allows representing the ``Time`` object in the desired\noutput ``format`` and optional sub-format ``subfmt``.  Available\nbuilt-in formats include ``jd``, ``mjd``, ``iso``, and so forth. Each\nformat can have its own sub-formats\n\nFor bu", "start_line": 926, "end_line": 1005, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "value", "qualified_name": "value", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Time value(s) in current format.", "start_line": 1008, "end_line": 1010, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "masked", "qualified_name": "masked", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1013, "end_line": 1014, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "mask", "qualified_name": "mask", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1017, "end_line": 1018, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "insert", "qualified_name": "insert", "args": ["self", "obj", "values", "axis"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Insert values before the given indices in the column and return\na new `~astropy.time.Time` or  `~astropy.time.TimeDelta` object.\n\nThe values to be inserted must conform to the rules for in-place setting\nof ``Time`` objects (see ``Get and set values`` in the ``Time``\ndocumentation).\n\nThe API signatur", "start_line": 1020, "end_line": 1096, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setitem__", "qualified_name": "__setitem__", "args": ["self", "item", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1098, "end_line": 1128, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "isclose", "qualified_name": "isclose", "args": ["self", "other", "atol"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a boolean or boolean array where two Time objects are\nelement-wise equal within a time tolerance.\n\nThis evaluates the expression below::\n\n  abs(self - other) <= atol\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : `~astropy.time.Time`\n    Time object for comparison.\natol : `~astropy.units.Quantity` or `~astr", "start_line": 1130, "end_line": 1171, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self", "format"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a fully independent copy the Time object, optionally changing\nthe format.\n\nIf ``format`` is supplied then the time format of the returned Time\nobject will be set accordingly, otherwise it will be unchanged from the\noriginal.\n\nIn this method a full copy of the internal time arrays will be made", "start_line": 1173, "end_line": 1196, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "replicate", "qualified_name": "replicate", "args": ["self", "format", "copy", "cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a replica of the Time object, optionally changing the format.\n\nIf ``format`` is supplied then the time format of the returned Time\nobject will be set accordingly, otherwise it will be unchanged from the\noriginal.\n\nIf ``copy`` is set to `True` then a full copy of the internal time arrays\nwill ", "start_line": 1198, "end_line": 1227, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_apply", "qualified_name": "_apply", "args": ["self", "method"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new time object, possibly applying a method to the arrays.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmethod : str or callable\n    If string, can be 'replicate'  or the name of a relevant\n    `~numpy.ndarray` method. In the former case, a new time instance\n    with unchanged internal data is created, while in ", "start_line": 1229, "end_line": 1336, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__copy__", "qualified_name": "__copy__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overrides the default behavior of the `copy.copy` function in\nthe python stdlib to behave like `Time.copy`. Does *not* make a\ncopy of the JD arrays - only copies by reference.", "start_line": 1338, "end_line": 1344, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__deepcopy__", "qualified_name": "__deepcopy__", "args": ["self", "memo"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overrides the default behavior of the `copy.deepcopy` function\nin the python stdlib to behave like `Time.copy`. Does make a\ncopy of the JD arrays.", "start_line": 1346, "end_line": 1352, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_advanced_index", "qualified_name": "_advanced_index", "args": ["self", "indices", "axis", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Turn argmin, argmax output into an advanced index.\n\nArgmin, argmax output contains indices along a given axis in an array\nshaped like the other dimensions.  To use this to get values at the\ncorrect location, a list is constructed in which the other axes are\nindexed sequentially.  For ``keepdims`` is", "start_line": 1354, "end_line": 1404, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "argmin", "qualified_name": "argmin", "args": ["self", "axis", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return indices of the minimum values along the given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.argmin`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2``\nis used.  See :func:`~numpy.argmin` for detailed documentation.", "start_line": 1406, "end_line": 1427, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "argmax", "qualified_name": "argmax", "args": ["self", "axis", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return indices of the maximum values along the given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.argmax`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2``\nis used.  See :func:`~numpy.argmax` for detailed documentation.", "start_line": 1429, "end_line": 1442, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "argsort", "qualified_name": "argsort", "args": ["self", "axis", "kind"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the indices that would sort the time array.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.argsort`, but adapted to ensure that\nthe full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2`` is used, and\nthat corresponding attributes are copied.  Internally, it uses\n:func:`~numpy.lexsort`, and h", "start_line": 1444, "end_line": 1475, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "min", "qualified_name": "min", "args": ["self", "axis", "out", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Minimum along a given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.min`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2``\nis used, and that corresponding attributes are copied.\n\nNote that the ``out`` argument is present only for compatibility with\n``np.mi", "start_line": 1477, "end_line": 1493, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "max", "qualified_name": "max", "args": ["self", "axis", "out", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Maximum along a given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.max`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2``\nis used, and that corresponding attributes are copied.\n\nNote that the ``out`` argument is present only for compatibility with\n``np.ma", "start_line": 1495, "end_line": 1511, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ptp", "qualified_name": "ptp", "args": ["self", "axis", "out", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Peak to peak (maximum - minimum) along a given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.ptp`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2``\nis used.\n\nNote that the ``out`` argument is present only for compatibility with\n`~numpy.ptp`; since `Time` i", "start_line": 1513, "end_line": 1529, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sort", "qualified_name": "sort", "args": ["self", "axis"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a copy sorted along the specified axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.sort`, but internally uses\nindexing with :func:`~numpy.lexsort` to ensure that the full precision\ngiven by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2`` is kept, and that\ncorresponding attributes are properly sorted and c", "start_line": 1531, "end_line": 1545, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "mean", "qualified_name": "mean", "args": ["self", "axis", "dtype", "out", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Mean along a given axis.\n\nThis is similar to :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.mean`, but adapted to ensure\nthat the full precision given by the two doubles ``jd1`` and ``jd2`` is\nused, and that corresponding attributes are copied.\n\nNote that the ``out`` argument is present only for compatibility with\n``np.mean", "start_line": 1547, "end_line": 1623, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cache", "qualified_name": "cache", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the cache associated with this instance.", "start_line": 1626, "end_line": 1630, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cache", "qualified_name": "cache", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cache.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1633, "end_line": 1634, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getattr__", "qualified_name": "__getattr__", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get dynamic attributes to output format or do timescale conversion.", "start_line": 1636, "end_line": 1671, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__dir__", "qualified_name": "__dir__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1673, "end_line": 1674, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_match_shape", "qualified_name": "_match_shape", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Ensure that `val` is matched to length of self.  If val has length 1\nthen broadcast, otherwise cast to double and make sure shape matches.", "start_line": 1676, "end_line": 1693, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_time_comparison", "qualified_name": "_time_comparison", "args": ["self", "other", "op"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If other is of same class as self, compare difference in self.scale.\nOtherwise, return NotImplemented.", "start_line": 1695, "end_line": 1722, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__lt__", "qualified_name": "__lt__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1724, "end_line": 1725, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__le__", "qualified_name": "__le__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1727, "end_line": 1728, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__eq__", "qualified_name": "__eq__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If other is an incompatible object for comparison, return `False`.\nOtherwise, return `True` if the time difference between self and\nother is zero.", "start_line": 1730, "end_line": 1736, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__ne__", "qualified_name": "__ne__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If other is an incompatible object for comparison, return `True`.\nOtherwise, return `False` if the time difference between self and\nother is zero.", "start_line": 1738, "end_line": 1744, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__gt__", "qualified_name": "__gt__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": 