t cosmologies.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmeta : mapping or None (optional, keyword-only)\n    Metadata that will ", "start_line": 175, "end_line": 237, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_init_arguments", "qualified_name": "_init_arguments", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 240, "end_line": 248, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_equivalent", "qualified_name": "is_equivalent", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check equivalence between Cosmologies.\n\nTwo cosmologies may be equivalent even if not the same class.\nFor example, an instance of ``LambdaCDM`` might have :math:`\\Omega_0=1`\nand :math:`\\Omega_k=0` and therefore be flat, like ``FlatLambdaCDM``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : `~astropy.cosmology.Cosmo", "start_line": 253, "end_line": 330, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__equiv__", "qualified_name": "__equiv__", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Cosmology equivalence. Use ``.is_equivalent()`` for actual check!\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : `~astropy.cosmology.Cosmology` subclass instance, positional-only\n    The object in which to compare.\n\nReturns\n-------\nbool or `NotImplemented`\n    `NotImplemented` if ``other`` is from a different class", "start_line": 332, "end_line": 356, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__eq__", "qualified_name": "__eq__", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check equality between Cosmologies.\n\nChecks the Parameters and immutable fields (i.e. not \"meta\").\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : `~astropy.cosmology.Cosmology` subclass instance, positional-only\n    The object in which to compare.\n\nReturns\n-------\nbool\n    `True` if Parameters and names are the sam", "start_line": 358, "end_line": 389, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 393, "end_line": 400,