ns pixel\narea of the image pixel at the ``CRPIX`` location once it is projected\nonto the \"plane of intermediate world coordinates\" as defined in\n`Greisen & Calabretta 2002, A&A, 395, 1061 <https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2002A%26A...3", "start_line": 2728, "end_line": 2773, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_fits", "qualified_name": "to_fits", "args": ["self", "relax", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate an `~astropy.io.fits.HDUList` object with all of the\ninformation stored in this object.  This should be logically identical\nto the input FITS file, but it will be normalized in a number of ways.\n\nSee `to_header` for some warnings about the output produced.\n\nParameters\n----------\nrelax : boo", "start_line": 2775, "end_line": 2814, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_header", "qualified_name": "to_header", "args": ["self", "relax", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate an `astropy.io.fits.Header` object with the basic WCS\nand SIP information stored in this object.  This should be\nlogically identical to the input FITS file, but it will be\nnormalized in a number of ways.\n\n.. warning::\n\n  This function does not write out FITS WCS `distortion\n  paper`_ inform", "start_line": 2816, "end_line": 2979, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_fix_ctype", "qualified_name": "_fix_ctype", "args": ["self", "header", "add_sip", "log_message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\nheader : `~astropy.io.fits.Header`\n    FITS header.\nadd_sip : bool\n    Flag indicating whether \"-SIP\" should be added or removed from CTYPE keywords.\n\n    Remove \"-SIP\" from CTYPE when writing out a header with relax=False.\n    This needs to be done outside ``to_header`` becaus", "start_line": 2981, "end_line": 3029, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_header_string", "qualified_name": "to_header_string", "args": ["self", "relax"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Identical to `to_header`, but returns a string containing the\nheader cards.", "start_line": 3031, "end_line": 3036, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "footprint_to_file", "qualified_name": "footprint_to_file", "args": ["self", "filename", "color", "width", "coordsys"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Writes out a `ds9`_ style regions file. It can be loaded\ndirectly by `ds9`_.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : str, optional\n    Output file name - default is ``'footprint.reg'``\n\ncolor : str, optional\n    Color to use when plotting the line.\n\nwidth : int, optional\n    Width of the region line.\n\ncoo", "start_line": 3038, "end_line": 3097, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_naxis", "qualified_name": "_get_naxis", "args": ["self", "header"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3099, "end_line": 3111, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "printwcs", "qualified_name": "printwcs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3113, "end_line": 3114, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a short description. Simply porting the behavior from\nthe `printwcs()` method.", "start_line": 3116, "end_line": 3147, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_axis_types", "qualified_name": "get_axis_types", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Similar to `self.wcsprm.axis_types <astropy.wcs.Wcsprm.axis_types>`\nbut provides the information in a more Python-friendly format.\n\nReturns\n-------\nresult : list of dict\n\n    Returns a list of dictionaries, one for each axis, each\n    containing attributes about the type of that axis.\n\n    Each dict", "start_line": 3149, "end_line": 3240, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Support pickling of WCS objects.  This is done by serializing\nto an in-memory FITS file and dumping that as a string.", "start_line": 3242, "end_line": 3262, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dropaxis", "qualified_name": "dropaxis", "args": ["self", "dropax"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove an axis from the WCS.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwcs : `~astropy.wcs.WCS`\n    The WCS with naxis to be chopped to naxis-1\ndropax : int\n    The index of the WCS to drop, counting from 0 (i.e., python convention,\n    not FITS convention)\n\nReturns\n-------\n`~astropy.wcs.WCS`\n    A new `~astropy.wcs.W", "start_line": 3264, "end_line": 3287, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "swapaxes", "qualified_name": "swapaxes", "args": ["self", "ax0", "ax1"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Swap axes in a WCS.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwcs : `~astropy.wcs.WCS`\n    The WCS to have its axes swapped\nax0 : int\nax1 : int\n    The indices of the WCS to be swapped, counting from 0 (i.e., python\n    convention, not FITS convention)\n\nReturns\n-------\n`~astropy.wcs.WCS`\n    A new `~astropy.wcs.WCS` i", "start_line": 3289, "end_line": 3311, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reorient_celestial_first", "qualified_name": "reorient_celestial_first", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reorient the WCS such that the celestial axes are first, followed by\nthe spectral axis, followed by any others.\nAssumes at least celestial axes are present.", "start_line": 3313, "end_line": 3321, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "slice", "qualified_name": "slice", "args": ["self", "view", "numpy_order"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Slice a WCS instance using a Numpy slice. The order of the slice should\nbe reversed (as for the data) compared to the natural WCS order.\n\nParameters\n----------\nview : tuple\n    A tuple containing the same number of slices as the WCS system.\n    The ``step`` method, the third argument to a slice, is ", "start_line": 3323, "end_line": 3422, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3424, "end_line": 3429, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3431, "end_line": 3435, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "axis_type_names", "qualified_name": "axis_type_names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "World names for each coordinate axis.\n\nReturns\n-------\nlist of str\n    A list of names along each axis.", "start_line": 3438, "end_line": 3453, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "celestial", "qualified_name": "celestial", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A copy of the current WCS with only the celestial axes included.", "start_line": 3456, "end_line": 3460, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_celestial", "qualified_name": "is_celestial", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3463, "end_line": 3464, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_celestial", "qualified_name": "has_celestial", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3467, "end_line": 3471, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "spectral", "qualified_name": "spectral", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A copy of the current WCS with only the spectral axes included.", "start_line": 3474, "end_line": 3478, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_spectral", "qualified_name": "is_spectral", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3481, "end_line": 3482, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_spectral", "qualified_name": "has_spectral", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 3485,