te", "sum_of_implicit_terms", "fit_deriv", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "Shift a coordinate.\n\nParameters\n----------\noffset : float\n    Offset to add to a coordinate.", "start_line": 559, "end_line": 614}, {"name": "Scale", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["input_units", "inverse", "evaluate", "fit_deriv", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "Multiply a model by a dimensionless factor.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfactor : float\n    Factor by which to scale a coordinate.\n\nNotes\n-----\nIf ``factor`` is a `~astropy.units.Quantity` then the units will be\nstripped before the scaling operation.", "start_line": 617, "end_line": 680}, {"name": "Multiply", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["inverse", "evaluate", "fit_deriv", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "Multiply a model by a quantity or number.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfactor : float\n    Factor by which to multiply a coordinate.", "start_line": 683, "end_line": 728}, {"name": "RedshiftScaleFactor", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["evaluate", "fit_deriv", "inverse"], "docstring": "One dimensional redshift scale factor model.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : float\n    Redshift value.\n\nNotes\n-----\nModel formula:\n\n    .. math:: f(x) = x (1 + z)", "start_line": 731, "end_line": 777}, {"name": "Sersic1D", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["evaluate", "input_units", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "One dimensional Sersic surface brightness profile.\n\nParameters\n----------\namplitude : float\n    Surface brightness at r_eff.\nr_eff : float\n    Effective (half-light) radius\nn : float\n    Sersic Index.\n\nSee Also\n--------\nGaussian1D, Moffat1D, Lorentz1D\n\nNotes\n-----\nModel formula:\n\n.. math::\n\n    I(r)", "start_line": 780, "end_line": 871}, {"name": "_Trigonometric1D", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["input_units", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "Base class for one dimensi