1093, "end_line": 1375}, {"name": "LevMarLSQFitter", "bases": ["_NonLinearLSQFitter"], "methods": ["__init__", "_run_fitter"], "docstring": "Levenberg-Marquardt algorithm and least squares statistic.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncalc_uncertainties : bool\n    If the covarience matrix should be computed and set in the fit_info.\n    Default: False\n\nAttributes\n----------\nfit_info : dict\n    The `scipy.optimize.leastsq` result for the most recent f", "start_line": 1378, "end_line": 1455}, {"name": "_NLLSQFitter", "bases": ["_NonLinearLSQFitter"], "methods": ["__init__", "_run_fitter"], "docstring": "Wrapper class for `scipy.optimize.least_squares` method, which provides:\n    - Trust Region Reflective\n    - dogbox\n    - Levenberg-Marqueardt\nalgorithms using the least squares statistic.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmethod : str\n    \u2018trf\u2019 :  Trust Region Reflective algorithm, particularly suitable\n     ", "start_line": 1458, "end_line": 1553}, {"name": "TRFLSQFitter", "bases": ["_NLLSQFitter"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Trust Region Reflective algorithm and least squares statistic.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncalc_uncertainties : bool\n    If the covarience matrix should be computed and set in the fit_info.\n    Default: False\nuse_min_max_bounds: bool\n    If the set parameter bounds for a model will be enforced each given", "start_line": 1556, "end_line": 1579}, {"name": "DogBoxLSQFitter", "bases": ["_NLLSQFitter"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "DogBox algorithm and least squares statistic.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncalc_uncertainties : bool\n    If the covarience matrix should be computed and set in the fit_info.\n    Default: False\nuse_min_max_bounds: bool\n    If the set parameter bounds for a model will be enforced each given\n    parameter wh", "start_line": 1582, "end_line": 1605}, {"name": "LMLSQFitter", "bases": ["_NLLSQFitter"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "`scipy.optimize.least_squares` Levenberg-Marquardt algorithm and least squares statistic.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncalc_uncertainties : bool\n    If the covarience matrix should be computed and set in the fit_info.\n    Default: False\n\nAttributes\n----------\nfit_info :\n    A `scipy.optimize.OptimizeResul", "start_line": 1608, "end_line": 1626}, {"name": "SLSQPLSQFitter", "bases": ["Fitter"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__"], "docstring": "Sequential Least Squares Programming (SLSQP) optimization algorithm and\nleast squares statistic.\n\nRaises\n------\nModelLinearityError\n    A linear model is passed to a nonlinear fitter\n\nNotes\n-----\nSee also the `~astropy.modeling.optimizers.SLSQP` optimizer.", "start_line": 1629, "end_line": 1706}, {"name": "SimplexLSQFitter", "bases": ["Fitter"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__"], "docstring": "Simplex algorithm and least squares statistic.\n\nRaises\n------\n`ModelLinearityError`\n    A linear model is passed to a nonlinear fitter", "start_line": 1709, "end_line": 1776}, {"name": "JointFitter", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "model_to_fit_params", "objective_function", "_verify_input", "__call__"], "docstring": "Fit models which share a parameter.\nFor example, fit two gaussians to two data sets but keep\nthe FWHM the same.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodels : list\n    a list of model instances\njointparameters : list\n    a list of joint parameters\ninitvals : list\n    a list of initial values", "start_line": 1779, "end_line": 1929}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module implements classes (called Fitters) which combine optimization\nalgorithms (typically from `scipy.optimize`) with statistic functions to perform\nfitting. Fitters are implemented as callable classes. In addition to the data\nto fit, the ``__call__`` method takes an instance of\n`~astropy.modeling.core.FittableModel` as input, and returns a copy of the\nmodel with its parameters determined by the optimizer.\n\nOptimization algorithms, called \"optimizers\" are implemented in\n`~astropy.modeling.optimizers` and statistic functions are in\n`~astropy.modeling.statistic`. The goal is to provide an easy to extend\nframework and allow users to easily create new fitters by combining statistics\nwith optimizers.\n\nThere are two exceptions to the above scheme.\n`~astropy.modeling.fitting.LinearLSQFitter` uses Numpy's `~numpy.linalg.lstsq`\nfunction.  `~astropy.modeling.fitting.LevMarLSQFitter` uses\n`~scipy.optimize.leastsq` which combines optimization and statistic in one\nimplementation.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/spline.py", "file_hash": "8d7f21a178d9240d59e3801757e97162b90be06414429ec520ebb486241a93f4", "imports": [{"module": "abc", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "functools", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy.utils", "names": ["isiterable"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["FittableModel", "ModelDefinitionError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "parameters", "names": ["Parameter"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["BSpline"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["BSpline"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["InterpolatedUnivariateSpline"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["UnivariateSpline"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["LSQUnivariateSpline"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.interpolate", "names": ["splrep"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "knots", "coeffs", "degree", "bounds", "n_models", "model_set