y indicates all the left/right choices necessary to reach that node.\nEach key will reference a tuple that contains:\n\n- reference to the compound model for that node.\n- left most index contained within that subtree\n   (relative to all indices for the ", "start_line": 4204, "end_line": 4223, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fix_inputs", "qualified_name": "fix_inputs", "args": ["modelinstance", "values", "bounding_boxes", "selector_args"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This function creates a compound model with one or more of the input\nvalues of the input model assigned fixed values (scalar or array).\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodelinstance : `~astropy.modeling.Model` instance\n    This is the model that one or more of the\n    model input values will be fixed to some", "start_line": 4234, "end_line": 4270, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bind_bounding_box", "qualified_name": "bind_bounding_box", "args": ["modelinstance", "bounding_box", "ignored", "order"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set a validated bounding box to a model instance.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodelinstance : `~astropy.modeling.Model` instance\n    This is the model that the validated bounding box will be set on.\nbounding_box : tuple\n    A bounding box tuple, see :ref:`astropy:bounding-boxes` for details\nignored : lis", "start_line": 4273, "end_line": 4291, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bind_compound_bounding_box", "qualified_name": "bind_compound_bounding_box", "args": ["modelinstance", "bounding_boxes", "selector_args", "create_selector", "ignored", "order"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add a validated compound bounding box to a model instance.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodelinstance : `~astropy.modeling.Model` instance\n    This is the model that the validated compound bounding box will be set on.\nbounding_boxes : dict\n    A dictionary of bounding box tuples, see :ref:`astropy:boundin", "start_line": 4294, "end_line": 4334, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "custom_model", "qualified_name": "custom_model", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a model from a user defined function. The inputs and parameters of\nthe model will be inferred from the arguments of the function.\n\nThis can be used either as a function or as a decorator.  See below for\nexamples of both usages.\n\nThe model is separable only if there is a single input.\n\n.. note", "start_line": 4337, "end_line": 4424, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_custom_model_inputs", "qualified_name": "_custom_model_inputs", "args": ["func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Processes the inputs to the `custom_model`'s function into the appropriate\ncategories.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfunc : callable\n\nReturns\n-------\ninputs : list\n    list of evaluation inputs\nspecial_params : dict\n    dictionary of model properties which require special treatment\nsettable_params : dict\n ", "start_line": 4427, "end_line": 4476, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_custom_model_wrapper", "qualified_name": "_custom_model_wrapper", "args": ["func", "fit_deriv"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal implementation `custom_model`.\n\nWhen `custom_model` is called as a function its arguments are passed to\nthis function, and the result of this function is returned.\n\nWhen `custom_model` is used as a decorator a partial evaluation of this\nfunction is returned by `custom_model`.", "start_line": 4479, "end_line": 4534, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "render_model", "qualified_name": "render_model", "args": ["model", "arr", "coords"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluates a model on an input array. Evaluation is limited to\na bounding box if the `Model.bounding_box` attribute is set.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `Model`\n    Model to be evaluated.\narr : `numpy.ndarray`, optional\n    Array on which the model is evaluated.\ncoords : array-like, optional\n    Co", "start_line": 4537, "end_line": 4633, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "hide_inverse", "qualified_name": "hide_inverse", "args": ["model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This is a convenience function intended to disable automatic generation\nof the inverse in compound models by disabling one of the constituent\nmodel's inverse. This is to handle cases where user provided inverse\nfunctions are not compatible within an expression.\n\nFor example::\n\n    compound_model.inv", "start_line": 4636, "end_line": 4656, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__new__", "qualified_name": "__new__", "args": ["mcls", "name", "bases", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 106, "end_line": 148, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["cls", "name", "bases", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 150, "end_line": 160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Custom repr for Model subclasses.", "start_line": 162, "end_line": 166, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_repr_pretty_", "qualified_name": "_repr_pretty_", "args": ["cls", "p", "cycle"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Repr for IPython's pretty printer.\n\nBy default IPython \"pretty prints\" classes, so we need to implement\nthis so that IPython displays the custom repr for Models.", "start_line": 168, "end_line": 175, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 177, "end_line": 194, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The name of this model class--equivalent to ``cls.__name__``.\n\nThis attribute is provided for symmetry with the `Model.name` attribute\nof model instances.", "start_line": 197, "end_line": 204, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_is_concrete", "qualified_name": "_is_concrete", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A class-level property that determines whether the class is a concrete\nimplementation of a Model--i.e. it is not some abstract base class or\ninternal implementation detail (i.e. begins with '_').", "start_line": 207, "end_line": 213, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "rename", "qualified_name": "rename", "args": ["cls", "name", "inputs", "outputs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Creates a copy of this model class with a new name, inputs or outputs.\n\nThe new class is technically a subclass of the original class, so that\ninstance and type checks will still work.  For example::\n\n    >>> from astropy.modeling.models import Rotation2D\n    >>> SkyRotation = Rotation2D.rename('Sky", "start_line": 215, "end_line": 262, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_inverse_property", "qualified_name": "_create_inverse_property", "args": ["cls", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 264, "end_line": 281, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_bounding_box_property", "qualified_name": "_create_bounding_box_property", "args": ["cls", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Takes any bounding_box defined on a concrete Model subclass (either\nas a fixed tuple or a property or method) and wraps it in the generic\ngetter/setter interface for the bounding_box attribute.", "start_line": 283, "end_line": 321, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_bounding_box_subclass", "qualified_name": "_create_bounding_box_subclass", "args": ["cls", "func", "sig"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "For Models that take optional arguments for defining their bounding\nbox, we create a subclass of ModelBoundingBox with a ``__call__`` method\nthat supports those additional arguments.\n\nTakes the function's Signature as an argument since that is already\ncomputed in _create_bounding_box_property, so no", "start_line": 323, "end_line": 369, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_special_methods", "qualified_name": "_handle_special_methods", "args": ["cls", "members", "pdict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 371, "end_line": 461, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_format_cls_repr", "qualified_name": "_format_cls_repr", "args": ["cls", "keywords"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal implementation of ``__repr__``.\n\nThis is separated out for ease of use by subclasses that wish to\noverride the default ``__repr__`` while keeping the same basic\nformatting.", "start_line": 475, "end_line": 520, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init_subclass__", "qualified_name": "__init_subclass__", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 720, "end_line": 721, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 723, "end_line": 746, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_default_inputs_outputs", "qualified_name": "_default_inputs_outputs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 748, "end_line": 764, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_initialize_setters", "qualified_name": "_initialize_setters", "args": ["self", "kwargs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This exists to inject defaults for settable properties for models\noriginating from `custom_model`.", "start_line": 766, "end_line": 779, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inputs", "qualified_name": "inputs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 782, "end_line": 783, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inputs", "qualified_name": "inputs", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": ["inputs.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 786, "end_line": 792, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "outputs", "qualified_name": "outputs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 795, "end_line": 796, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "outputs", "qualified_name": "outputs", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": ["outputs.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 799, "end_line": 804, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "n_inputs", "qualified_name": "n_inputs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 807, "end_line": 821, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "n_outputs", "qualified_name": "n_outputs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 824, "end_line": 838, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_calculate_separability_matrix", "qualified_name": "_calculate_separability_matrix", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This is a hook which customises the behavior of modeling.separable.\n\nThis allows complex subclasses to customise the separability matrix.\nIf it returns `NotImplemented` the default behavior is used.", "start_line": 840, "end_line": 847, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_initialize_unit_support", "qualified_name": "_initialize_unit_support", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert self._input_units_strict and\nself.input_units_allow_dimensionless to dictionaries\nmapping input name to a boolean value.", "start_line": 849, "end_line": 863, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_units_strict", "qualified_name": "input_units_strict", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Enforce strict units on inputs to evaluate. If this is set to True,\ninput values to evaluate will be in the exact units specified by\ninput_units. If the input quantities are convertible to input_units,\nthey are converted. If this is a dictionary then it should map input\nname to a bool to set strict ", "start_line": 866, "end_line": 877, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_units_allow_dimensionless", "qualified_name": "input_units_allow_dimensionless", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Allow dimensionless input (and corresponding output). If this is True,\ninput values to evaluate will gain the units specified in input_units. If\nthis is a dictionary then it should map input name to a bool to allow\ndimensionless numbers for that input.\nOnly has an effect if input_units is defined.", "start_line": 880, "end_line": 891, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "uses_quantity", "qualified_name": "uses_quantity", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "True if this model has been created with `~astropy.units.Quantity`\nobjects or if there are no parameters.\n\nThis can be used to determine if this model should be evaluated with\n`~astropy.units.Quantity` or regular floats.", "start_line": 894, "end_line": 903, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 905, "end_line": 906, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 908, "end_line": 909, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__len__", "qualified_name": "__len__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 911, "end_line": 912, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_strip_ones", "qualified_name": "_strip_ones", "args": ["intup"], "decorators": ["staticmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 915, "end_line": 916, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setattr__", "qualified_name": "__setattr__", "args": ["self", "attr", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 918, "end_line": 962, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_pre_evaluate", "qualified_name": "_pre_evaluate", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Model specific input setup that needs to occur prior to model evaluation.", "start_line": 964, "end_line": 977, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_bounding_box", "qualified_name": "get_bounding_box", "args": ["self", "with_bbox"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the ``bounding_box`` of a model if it exists or ``None``\notherwise.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwith_bbox :\n    The value of the ``with_bounding_box`` keyword argument\n    when calling the model. Default is `True` for usage when\n    looking up the model's ``bounding_box`` without risk of error.", "start_line": 979, "end_line": 1004, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_argnames", "qualified_name": "_argnames", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The inputs used to determine input_shape for bounding_box evaluation.", "start_line": 1007, "end_line": 1009, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_validate_input_shape", "qualified_name": "_validate_input_shape", "args": ["self", "_input", "idx", "argnames", "model_set_axis", "check_model_set_axis"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform basic validation of a single model input's shape.\n\nThe shape has the minimum dimensions for the given model_set_axis.\n\nReturns the shape of the input if validation succeeds.", "start_line": 1011, "end_line": 1043, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_validate_input_shapes", "qualified_name": "_validate_input_shapes", "args": ["self", "inputs", "argnames", "model_set_axis"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform basic validation of model inputs\n    --that they are mutually broadcastable and that they have\n    the minimum dimensions for the given model_set_axis.\n\nIf validation succeeds, returns the total shape that will result from\nbroadcasting the input arrays with each other.", "start_line": 1045, "end_line": 1070, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_shape", "qualified_name": "input_shape", "args": ["self", "inputs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get input shape for bounding_box evaluation.", "start_line": 1072, "end_line": 1074, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_generic_evaluate", "qualified_name": "_generic_evaluate", "args": ["self", "evaluate", "_inputs", "fill_value", "with_bbox"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generic model evaluation routine.\n\nSelects and evaluates model with or without bounding_box enforcement.", "start_line": 1076, "end_line": 1088, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_post_evaluate", "qualified_name": "_post_evaluate", "args": ["self", "inputs", "outputs", "broadcasted_shapes", "with_bbox"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Model specific post evaluation processing of outputs.", "start_line": 1090, "end_line": 1102, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bbox_with_units", "qualified_name": "bbox_with_units", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1105, "end_line": 1106, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluate this model using the given input(s) and the parameter values\nthat were specified when the model was instantiated.", "start_line": 1108, "end_line": 1130, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_renamed_inputs_as_positional", "qualified_name": "_get_renamed_inputs_as_positional", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1132, "end_line": 1195, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "User-provided name for this model instance.", "start_line": 1199, "end_line": 1201, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": ["name.setter"], "docstring": "Assign a (new) name to this model.", "start_line": 1204, "end_line": 1206, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "model_set_axis", "qualified_name": "model_set_axis", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The index of the model set axis--that is the axis of a parameter array\nthat pertains to which model a parameter value pertains to--as\nspecified when the model was initialized.\n\nSee the documentation on :ref:`astropy:modeling-model-sets`\nfor more details.", "start_line": 1209, "end_line": 1218, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "param_sets", "qualified_name": "param_sets", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return parameters as a pset.\n\nThis is a list with one item per parameter set, which is an array of\nthat parameter's values across all parameter sets, with the last axis\nassociated with the parameter set.", "start_line": 1221, "end_line": 1229, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "parameters", "qualified_name": "parameters", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A flattened array of all parameter values in all parameter sets.\n\nFittable parameters maintain this list and fitters modify it.", "start_line": 1232, "end_line": 1250, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "parameters", "qualified_name": "parameters", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["parameters.setter"], "docstring": "Assigning to this attribute updates the parameters array rather than\nreplacing it.", "start_line": 1253, "end_line": 1272, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sync_constraints", "qualified_name": "sync_constraints", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "This is a boolean property that indicates whether or not accessing constraints\nautomatically check the constituent models current values. It defaults to True\non creation of a model, but for fitting purposes it should be set to False\nfor performance reasons.", "start_line": 1275, "end_line": 1284, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sync_constraints", "qualified_name": "sync_constraints", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["sync_constraints.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1287, "end_line": 1290, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fixed", "qualified_name": "fixed", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A ``dict`` mapping parameter names to their fixed constraint.", "start_line": 1293, "end_line": 1299, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bounds", "qualified_name": "bounds", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A ``dict`` mapping parameter names to their upper and lower bounds as\n``(min, max)`` tuples or ``[min, max]`` lists.", "start_line": 1302, "end_line": 1309, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "tied", "qualified_name": "tied", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A ``dict`` mapping parameter names to their tied constraint.", "start_line": 1312, "end_line": 1318, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "eqcons", "qualified_name": "eqcons", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "List of parameter equality constraints.", "start_line": 1321, "end_line": 1323, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ineqcons", "qualified_name": "ineqcons", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "List of parameter inequality constraints.", "start_line": 1326, "end_line": 1328, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_inverse", "qualified_name": "has_inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns True if the model has an analytic or user\ninverse defined.", "start_line": 1330, "end_line": 1340, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns a new `~astropy.modeling.Model` instance which performs the\ninverse transform, if an analytic inverse is defined for this model.\n\nEven on models that don't have an inverse defined, this property can be\nset with a manually-defined inverse, such a pre-computed or\nexperimentally determined inve", "start_line": 1343, "end_line": 1376, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["inverse.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1379, "end_line": 1387, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["inverse.deleter"], "docstring": "Resets the model's inverse to its default (if one exists, otherwise\nthe model will have no inverse).", "start_line": 1390, "end_line": 1398, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_user_inverse", "qualified_name": "has_user_inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A flag indicating whether or not a custom inverse model has been\nassigned to this model by a user, via assignment to ``model.inverse``.", "start_line": 1401, "end_line": 1406, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bounding_box", "qualified_name": "bounding_box", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A `tuple` of length `n_inputs` defining the bounding box limits, or\nraise `NotImplementedError` for no bounding_box.\n\nThe default limits are given by a ``bounding_box`` property or method\ndefined in the class body of a specific model.  If not defined then\nthis property just raises `NotImplementedErr", "start_line": 1409, "end_line": 1490, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bounding_box", "qualified_name": "bounding_box", "args": ["self", "bounding_box"], "decorators": ["bounding_box.setter"], "docstring": "Assigns the bounding box limits.", "start_line": 1493, "end_line": 1517, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": 