ass descriptors.", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 63}, {"name": "PolynomialModel", "bases": ["PolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "degree", "get_num_coeff", "_invlex", "_generate_coeff_names"], "docstring": "Base class for polynomial models.\n\nIts main purpose is to determine how many coefficients are needed\nbased on the polynomial order and dimension and to provide their\ndefault values, names and ordering.", "start_line": 66, "end_line": 143}, {"name": "_PolyDomainWindow1D", "bases": ["PolynomialModel"], "methods": ["__init__", "window", "window", "domain", "domain", "_set_default_domain_window", "__repr__", "__str__"], "docstring": "This class sets ``domain`` and ``window`` of 1D polynomials.", "start_line": 146, "end_line": 204}, {"name": "OrthoPolynomialBase", "bases": ["PolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "x_domain", "x_domain", "y_domain", "y_domain", "x_window", "x_window", "y_window", "y_window", "__repr__", "__str__", "get_num_coeff", "_invlex", "invlex_coeff", "_alpha", "imhorner", "_generate_coeff_names", "_fcache", "evaluate", "prepare_inputs"], "docstring": "This is a base class for the 2D Chebyshev and Legendre models.\n\nThe polynomials implemented here require a maximum degree in x and y.\n\nFor explanation of ``x_domain``, ``y_domain``, ```x_window`` and ```y_window``\nsee :ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window <astropy:domain-window-note>`.\n\n\n", "start_line": 207, "end_line": 454}, {"name": "Chebyshev1D", "bases": ["_PolyDomainWindow1D"], "methods": ["__init__", "fit_deriv", "prepare_inputs", "evaluate", "clenshaw"], "docstring": "Univariate Chebyshev series.\n\nIt is defined as:\n\n.. math::\n\n    P(x) = \\sum_{i=0}^{i=n}C_{i} * T_{i}(x)\n\nwhere ``T_i(x)`` is the corresponding Chebyshev polynomial of the 1st kind.\n\nFor explanation of ```domain``, and ``window`` see\n:ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window <domain-window-not", "start_line": 457, "end_line": 575}, {"name": "Hermite1D", "bases": ["_PolyDomainWindow1D"], "methods": ["__init__", "fit_deriv", "prepare_inputs", "evaluate", "clenshaw"], "docstring": "Univariate Hermite series.\n\nIt is defined as:\n\n.. math::\n\n    P(x) = \\sum_{i=0}^{i=n}C_{i} * H_{i}(x)\n\nwhere ``H_i(x)`` is the corresponding Hermite polynomial (\"Physicist's kind\").\n\nFor explanation of ``domain``, and ``window`` see\n:ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window <domain-window-not", "start_line": 578, "end_line": 697}, {"name": "Hermite2D", "bases": ["OrthoPolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "_fcache", "fit_deriv", "_hermderiv1d"], "docstring": "Bivariate Hermite series.\n\nIt is defined as\n\n.. math:: P_{nm}(x,y) = \\sum_{n,m=0}^{n=d,m=d}C_{nm} H_n(x) H_m(y)\n\nwhere ``H_n(x)`` and ``H_m(y)`` are Hermite polynomials.\n\nFor explanation of ``x_domain``, ``y_domain``, ``x_window`` and ``y_window``\nsee :ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window", "start_line": 700, "end_line": 844}, {"name": "Legendre1D", "bases": ["_PolyDomainWindow1D"], "methods": ["__init__", "prepare_inputs", "evaluate", "fit_deriv", "clenshaw"], "docstring": "Univariate Legendre series.\n\nIt is defined as:\n\n.. math::\n\n    P(x) = \\sum_{i=0}^{i=n}C_{i} * L_{i}(x)\n\nwhere ``L_i(x)`` is the corresponding Legendre polynomial.\n\nFor explanation of ``domain``, and ``window`` see\n:ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window <domain-window-note>`.\n\nParameters\n--", "start_line": 847, "end_line": 965}, {"name": "Polynomial1D", "bases": ["_PolyDomainWindow1D"], "methods": ["__init__", "prepare_inputs", "evaluate", "fit_deriv", "horner", "input_units", "_parameter_units_for_data_units"], "docstring": "1D Polynomial model.\n\nIt is defined as:\n\n.. math::\n\n    P = \\sum_{i=0}^{i=n}C_{i} * x^{i}\n\nFor explanation of ``domain``, and ``window`` see\n:ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window <domain-window-note>`.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndegree : int\n    degree of the series\ndomain : tuple or None, op", "start_line": 968, "end_line": 1090}, {"name": "Polynomial2D", "bases": ["PolynomialModel"], "methods": ["__init__", "prepare_inputs", "evaluate", "__repr__", "__str__", "fit_deriv", "invlex_coeff", "multivariate_horner", "input_units", "_parameter_units_for_data_units", "x_domain", "x_domain", "y_domain", "y_domain", "x_window", "x_window", "y_window", "y_window"], "docstring": "2D Polynomial  model.\n\nRepresents a general polynomial of degree n:\n\n.. math::\n\n    P(x,y) = c_{00} + c_{10}x + ...+ c_{n0}x^n + c_{01}y + ...+ c_{0n}y^n\n    + c_{11}xy + c_{12}xy^2 + ... + c_{1(n-1)}xy^{n-1}+ ... + c_{(n-1)1}x^{n-1}y\n\nFor explanation of ``x_domain``, ``y_domain``, ``x_window`` and ", "start_line": 1093, "end_line": 1352}, {"name": "Chebyshev2D", "bases": ["OrthoPolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "_fcache", "fit_deriv", "_chebderiv1d"], "docstring": "Bivariate Chebyshev series..\n\nIt is defined as\n\n.. math:: P_{nm}(x,y) = \\sum_{n,m=0}^{n=d,m=d}C_{nm}  T_n(x ) T_m(y)\n\nwhere ``T_n(x)`` and ``T_m(y)`` are Chebyshev polynomials of the first kind.\n\nFor explanation of ``x_domain``, ``y_domain``, ``x_window`` and ``y_window``\nsee :ref:`Notes regarding u", "start_line": 1355, "end_line": 1500}, {"name": "Legendre2D", "bases": ["OrthoPolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "_fcache", "fit_deriv", "_legendderiv1d"], "docstring": "Bivariate Legendre series.\n\nDefined as:\n\n.. math:: P_{n_m}(x,y) = \\sum_{n,m=0}^{n=d,m=d}C_{nm}  L_n(x ) L_m(y)\n\nwhere ``L_n(x)`` and ``L_m(y)`` are Legendre polynomials.\n\nFor explanation of ``x_domain``, ``y_domain``, ``x_window`` and ``y_window``\nsee :ref:`Notes regarding usage of domain and window", "start_line": 1503, "end_line": 1653}, {"name": "_SIP1D", "bases": ["PolynomialBase"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__", "__str__", "evaluate", "get_num_coeff", "_generate_coeff_names", "_coeff_matrix", "_eval_sip"], "docstring": "This implements the Simple Imaging Polynomial Model (SIP) in 1D.\n\nIt's unlikely it will be used in 1D so this class is private\nand SIP should be used instead.", "start_line": 1656, "end_line": 1766}, {"name": "SIP", "bases": ["Model"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__", "__str__", "inverse", "evaluate"], "docstring": "Simple Imaging Polynomial (SIP) model.\n\nThe SIP convention is used to represent distortions in FITS image headers.\nSee [1]_ for a description of the SIP convention.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncrpix : list or (2,) ndarray\n    CRPIX values\na_order : int\n    SIP polynomial order for first axis\nb_order : in", "start_line": 1769, "end_line": 1883}, {"name": "InverseSIP", "bases": ["Model"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__", "__str__", "evaluate"], "docstring": "Inverse Simple Imaging Polynomial.\n\nParameters\n----------\nap_order : int\n    order for the inverse transformation (AP coefficients)\nbp_order : int\n    order for the inverse transformation (BP coefficients)\nap_coeff : dict\n    coefficients for the inverse transform\nbp_coeff : dict\n    coefficients fo", "start_line": 1886, "end_line": 1955}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module contains models representing polynomials and polynomial series.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/powerlaws.py", "file_hash": "c70b88229a4b555a17242e466cd1c59f451b46e8446f0f37d831f94d33435645", "imports": [{"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy.units", "names": ["Magnitude", "Quantity", "UnitsError", "dimensionless_unscaled", "mag"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["Fittable1DModel"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "parameters", "names": ["InputParameterError", "Parameter"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "evaluate", "qualified_name": "evaluate", "args": ["x", "amplitude", "x_0", "alpha"], "decorators": ["staticmethod"], "docstring": "One dimensional power law model function.", "start_line": 53, "end_line": 56, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fit_deriv", "qualified_name"