ync": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_enabled_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "set_enabled_equivalencies", "args": ["equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Sets the equivalencies enabled in the unit registry.\n\nThese equivalencies are used if no explicit equivalencies are given,\nboth in unit conversion and in finding equivalent units.\n\nThis is meant in particular for allowing angles to be dimensionless.\nUse with care.\n\nParameters\n----------\nequivalencie", "start_line": 472, "end_line": 503, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_enabled_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "add_enabled_equivalencies", "args": ["equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Adds to the equivalencies enabled in the unit registry.\n\nThese equivalencies are used if no explicit equivalencies are given,\nboth in unit conversion and in finding equivalent units.\n\nThis is meant in particular for allowing angles to be dimensionless.\nSince no equivalencies are enabled by default, ", "start_line": 506, "end_line": 527, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_enabled_aliases", "qualified_name": "set_enabled_aliases", "args": ["aliases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set aliases for units.\n\nThis is useful for handling alternate spellings for units, or\nmisspelled units in files one is trying to read.\n\nParameters\n----------\naliases : dict of str, Unit\n    The aliases to set. The keys must be the string aliases, and values\n    must be the `astropy.units.Unit` that ", "start_line": 530, "end_line": 562, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_enabled_aliases", "qualified_name": "add_enabled_aliases", "args": ["aliases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add aliases for units.\n\nThis is useful for handling alternate spellings for units, or\nmisspelled units in files one is trying to read.\n\nSince no aliases are enabled by default, generally it is recommended\nto use `set_enabled_aliases`.\n\nParameters\n----------\naliases : dict of str, Unit\n    The aliase", "start_line": 565, "end_line": 600, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_recreate_irreducible_unit", "qualified_name": "_recreate_irreducible_unit", "args": ["cls", "names", "registered"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This is used to reconstruct units when passed around by\nmultiprocessing.", "start_line": 1889, "end_line": 1906, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_add_prefixes", "qualified_name": "_add_prefixes", "args": ["u", "excludes", "namespace", "prefixes"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set up all of the standard metric prefixes for a unit.  This\nfunction should not be used directly, but instead use the\n`prefixes` kwarg on `def_unit`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nexcludes : list of str, optional\n    Any prefixes to exclude from creation to avoid namespace\n    collisions.\n\nnamespace : dic", "start_line": 2492, "end_line": 2550, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "def_unit", "qualified_name": "def_unit", "args": ["s", "represents", "doc", "format", "prefixes", "exclude_prefixes", "namespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Factory function for defining new units.\n\nParameters\n----------\ns : str or list of str\n    The name of the unit.  If a list, the first element is the\n    canonical (short) name, and the rest of the elements are\n    aliases.\n\nrepresents : UnitBase instance, optional\n    The unit that this named unit ", "start_line": 2553, "end_line": 2626, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_condition_arg", "qualified_name": "_condition_arg", "args": ["value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Validate value is acceptable for conversion purposes.\n\nWill convert into an array if not a scalar, and can be converted\ninto an array\n\nParameters\n----------\nvalue : int or float value, or sequence of such values\n\nReturns\n-------\nScalar value or numpy array\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError\n    If value is n", "start_line": 2629, "end_li