 "qualified_name": "_is_equivalent", "args": ["self", "other", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns `True` if this unit is equivalent to `other`.\nSee `is_equivalent`, except that a proper Unit object should be\ngiven (i.e., no string) and that the equivalency list should be\nnormalized using `_normalize_equivalencies`.", "start_line": 1009, "end_line": 1037, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_apply_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "_apply_equivalencies", "args": ["self", "unit", "other", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal function (used from `_get_converter`) to apply\nequivalence pairs.", "start_line": 1039, "end_line": 1085, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_converter", "qualified_name": "_get_converter", "args": ["self", "other", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get a converter for values in ``self`` to ``other``.\n\nIf no conversion is necessary, returns ``unit_scale_converter``\n(which is used as a check in quantity helpers).", "start_line": 1087, "end_line": 1124, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_to", "qualified_name": "_to", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the scale to the specified unit.\n\nSee `to`, except that a Unit object should be given (i.e., no\nstring), and that all defaults are used, i.e., no\nequivalencies and value=1.", "start_line": 1126, "end_line": 1159, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to", "qualified_name": "to", "args": ["self", "other", "value", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the converted values in the specified unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : unit-like\n    The unit to convert to.\n\nvalue : int, float, or scalar array-like, optional\n    Value(s) in the current unit to be converted to the\n    specified unit.  If not provided, defaults to 1.0\n\nequivalencies : l", "start_line": 1161, "end_line": 1195, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "in_units", "qualified_name": "in_units", "args": ["self", "other", "value", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Alias for `to` for backward compatibility with pynbody.", "start_line": 1197, "end_line": 1201, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "decompose", "qualified_name": "decompose", "args": ["self", "bases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a unit object composed of only irreducible units.\n\nParameters\n----------\nbases : sequence of UnitBase, optional\n    The bases to decompose into.  When not provided,\n    decomposes down to any irreducible units.  When provided,\n    the decomposed result will only contain the given units.\n    T", "start_line": 1203, "end_line": 1221, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_compose", "qualified_name": "_compose", "args": ["self", "equivalencies", "namespace", "max_depth", "depth", "cached_results"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1223, "end_line": 1342, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "compose", "qualified_name": "compose", "args": ["self", "equivalencies", "units", "max_depth", "include_prefix_units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the simplest possible composite unit(s) that represent\nthe given unit.  Since there may be multiple equally simple\ncompositions of the unit, a list of units is always returned.\n\nParameters\n----------\nequivalencies : list of tuple\n    A list of equivalence pairs to also list.  See\n    :ref:`as", "start_line": 1344, "end_line": 1478, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_system", "qualified_name": "to_system", "args": ["self", "system"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Converts this unit into ones belonging to the given system.\nSince more than one result may be possible, a list is always\nreturned.\n\nParameters\n----------\nsystem : module\n    The module that defines the unit system.  Commonly used\n    ones include `astropy.units.si` and `astropy.units.cgs`.\n\n    To u", "start_line": 1480, "end_line": 1523, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "si", "qualified_name": "si", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "Returns a copy of the current `Unit` instance in SI units.", "start_line": 1526, "end_line": 1532, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cgs", "qualified_name": "cgs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "Returns a copy of the current `Unit` instance with CGS units.", "start_line": 1535, "end_line": 1541, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "physical_type", "qualified_name": "physical_type", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Physical type(s) dimensionally compatible with the unit.\n\nReturns\n-------\n`~astropy.units.physical.PhysicalType`\n    A representation of the physical type(s) of a unit.\n\nExamples\n--------\n>>> from astropy import units as u\n>>> u.m.physical_type\nPhysicalType('length')\n>>> (u.m ** 2 / u.s).physical_ty", "start_line": 1544, "end_line": 1580, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_units_with_same_physical_type", "qualified_name": "_get_units_with_same_physical_type", "args": ["self", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of registered units with the same physical type\nas this unit.\n\nThis function is used by Quantity to add its built-in\nconversions to equivalent units.\n\nThis is a private method, since end users should be encouraged\nto use the more powerful `compose` and `find_equivalent_units`\nmethods (", "start_line": 1582, "end_line": 1612, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "find_equivalent_units", "qualified_name": "find_equivalent_units", "args": ["self", "equivalencies", "units", "include_prefix_units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of all the units that are the same type as ``self``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nequivalencies : list of tuple\n    A list of equivalence pairs to also list.  See\n    :ref:`astropy:unit_equivalencies`.\n    Any list given, including an empty one, supersedes global defaults\n    that may be in ", "start_line": 1679, "end_line": 1716, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_unity", "qualified_name": "is_unity", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns `True` if the unit is unscaled and dimensionless.", "start_line": 1718, "end_line": 1722, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "st", "doc", "format", "namespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1765, "end_line": 1799, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_generate_doc", "qualified_name": "_generate_doc", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate a docstring for the unit if the user didn't supply\none.  This is only used from the constructor and may be\noverridden in subclasses.", "start_line": 1801, "end_line": 1811, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_format_name", "qualified_name": "get_format_name", "args": ["self", "format"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get a name for this unit that is specific to a particular\nformat.\n\nUses the dictionary passed into the `format` kwarg in the\nconstructor.\n\nParameters\n----------\nformat : str\n    The name of the format\n\nReturns\n-------\nname : str\n    The name of the unit for the given format.", "start_line": 1813, "end_line": 1831, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "names", "qualified_name": "names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns all of the names associated with this unit.", "start_line": 1834, "end_line": 1838, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns the canonical (short) name associated with this unit.", "start_line": 1841, "end_line": 1845, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "aliase