gs": ["self", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 573, "end_line": 598, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_wrap__", "qualified_name": "__array_wrap__", "args": ["self", "obj", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 600, "end_line": 610, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_ufunc__", "qualified_name": "__array_ufunc__", "args": ["self", "function", "method"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrap numpy ufuncs, taking care of units.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfunction : callable\n    ufunc to wrap.\nmethod : str\n    Ufunc method: ``__call__``, ``at``, ``reduce``, etc.\ninputs : tuple\n    Input arrays.\nkwargs : keyword arguments\n    As passed on, with ``out`` containing possible quantity output.", "start_line": 612, "end_line": 691, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_result_as_quantity", "qualified_name": "_result_as_quantity", "args": ["self", "result", "unit", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Turn result into a quantity with the given unit.\n\nIf no output is given, it will take a view of the array as a quantity,\nand set the unit.  If output is given, those should be quantity views\nof the result arrays, and the function will just set the unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nresult : ndarray or tup", "start_line": 693, "end_line": 743, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__quantity_subclass__", "qualified_name": "__quantity_subclass__", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overridden by subclasses to change what kind of view is\ncreated based on the output unit of an operation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : UnitBase\n    The unit for which the appropriate class should be returned\n\nReturns\n-------\ntuple :\n    - `~astropy.units.Quantity` subclass\n    - bool: True if subcl", "start_line": 745, "end_line": 761, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_new_view", "qualified_name": "_new_view", "args": ["self", "obj", "unit", "propagate_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a Quantity view of some array-like input, and set the unit.\n\nBy default, return a view of ``obj`` of the same class as ``self`` and\nwith the same unit.  Subclasses can override the type of class for a\ngiven unit using ``__quantity_subclass__``, and can ensure properties\nother than the unit ar", "start_line": 763, "end_line": 833, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_unit", "qualified_name": "_set_unit", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the unit.\n\nThis is used anywhere the unit is set or modified, i.e., in the\ninitializer, in ``__imul__`` and ``__itruediv__`` for in-place\nmultiplication and division by another unit, as well as in\n``__array_finalize__`` for wrapping up views.  For Quantity, it just\nsets the unit, but subclasses ", "start_line": 835, "end_line": 860, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__deepcopy__", "qualified_name": "__deepcopy__", "args": ["self", "memo"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 862, "end_line": 865, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 867, "end_line": 873, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setstate__", "qualified_name": "__setstate__", "args": ["self", "state"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 875, "end_line": 881, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_to_value", "qualified_name": "_to_value", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for to and to_value.", "start_line": 885, "end_line": 903, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to", "qualified_name": "to", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a new `~astropy.units.Quantity` object with the specified unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : unit-like\n    An object that represents the unit to convert to. Must be\n    an `~astropy.units.UnitBase` object or a string parseable\n    by the `~astropy.units` package.\n\nequivalencies : list of tup", "start_line": 905, "end_line": 942, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_value", "qualified_name": "to_value", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The numerical value, possibly in a different unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : unit-like, optional\n    The unit in which the value should be given. If not given or `None`,\n    use the current unit.\n\nequivalencies : list of tuple, optional\n    A list of equivalence pairs to try if the units are not", "start_line": 944, "end_line": 996, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A `~astropy.units.UnitBase` object representing the unit of this\nquantity.", "start_line": 1009, "end_line": 1014, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "equivalencies", "qualified_name": "equivalencies", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A list of equivalencies that will be applied by default during\nunit conversions.", "start_line": 1017, "end_line": 1022, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_recursively_apply", "qualified_name": "_recursively_apply", "args": ["self", "func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Apply function recursively to every field.\n\nReturns a copy with the result.", "start_line": 1024, "end_line": 1038, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "si", "qualified_name": "si", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns a copy of the current `Quantity` instance with SI units. The\nvalue of the resulting object will be scaled.", "start_line": 1041, "end_line": 1049, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cgs", "qualified_name": "cgs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], 