 or section associated with a particular\npackage or module.\n\nParameters\n----------\npackageormod : str or None\n    The package for which to retrieve the configuration object. If a\n    string, it must be a valid package name, or if ``None``, the package from\n    which this", "start_line": 522, "end_line": 603, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "generate_config", "qualified_name": "generate_config", "args": ["pkgname", "filename", "verbose"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generates a configuration file, from the list of `ConfigItem`\nobjects for each subpackage.\n\n.. versionadded:: 4.1\n\nParameters\n----------\npkgname : str or None\n    The package for which to retrieve the configuration object.\nfilename : str or file-like or None\n    If None, the default configuration pa", "start_line": 606, "end_line": 698, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload_config", "qualified_name": "reload_config", "args": ["packageormod", "rootname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reloads configuration settings from a configuration file for the root\npackage of the requested package/module.\n\nThis overwrites any changes that may have been made in `ConfigItem`\nobjects.  This applies for any items that are based on this file, which\nis determined by the *root* package of ``package", "start_line": 701, "end_line": 723, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_unedited_config_file", "qualified_name": "is_unedited_config_file", "args": ["content", "template_content"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines if a config file can be safely replaced because it doesn't\nactually contain any meaningful content, i.e. if it contains only comments\nor is completely empty.", "start_line": 726, "end_line": 735, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_default_config", "qualified_name": "update_default_config", "args": ["pkg", "default_cfg_dir_or_fn", "version", "rootname"], "decorators": ["deprecated('5.0')"], "docstring": "Checks if the configuration file for the specified package exists,\nand if not, copy over the default configuration.  If the\nconfiguration file looks like it has already been edited, we do\nnot write over it, but instead write a file alongside it named\n``pkg.version.cfg`` as a \"template\" for the user.", "start_line": 743, "end_line": 839, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "create_config_file", "qualified_name": "create_config_file", "args": ["pkg", "rootname", "overwrite"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create the default configuration file for the specified package.\nIf the file already exists, it is updated only if it has not been\nmodified.  Otherwise the ``overwrite`` flag is needed to overwrite it.\n\nParameters\n----------\npkg : str\n    The package to be updated.\nrootname : str\n    Name of the roo", "start_line": 842, "end_line": 895, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["cls", "name", "bases", "dict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 82, "end_line": 88, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 110, "end_line": 113, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "values", "qualified_name": "values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Iterate over configuration item values.", "start_line": 118, "end_line": 122, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "items", "qualified_name": "items", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Iterate over configuration item ``(name, value)`` pairs.", "start_line": 124, "end_line": 128, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_temp", "qualified_name": "set_temp", "args": ["self", "attr", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Temporarily set a configuration value.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str\n    Configuration item name\n\nvalue : object\n    The value to set temporarily.\n\nExamples\n--------\n>>> import astropy\n>>> with astropy.conf.set_temp('use_color', False):\n...     pass\n...     # console output will not contain colo", "start_line": 130, "end_line": 152, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload", "qualified_name": "reload", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reload a configuration item from the configuration file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str, optional\n    The name of the configuration parameter to reload.  If not\n    provided, reload all configuration parameters.", "start_line": 154, "end_line": 170, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reset", "qualified_name": "reset", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reset a configuration item to its default.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str, optional\n    The name of the configuration parameter to reload.  If not\n    provided, reset all configuration parameters.", "start_line": 172, "end_line": 190, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "defaultvalue", "description", "cfgtype", "module", "aliases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 258, "end_line": 303, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "obj", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 305, "end_line": 306, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__get__", "qualified_name": "__get__", "args": ["self", "obj", "objtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 308, "end_line": 311, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set", "qualified_name": "set", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Sets the current value of this ``ConfigItem``.\n\nThis also updates the comments that give the description and type\ninformation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nvalue\n    The value this item should be set to.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If the provided ``value`` is not valid for this ``ConfigItem``.", "start_line": 313, "end_line": 340, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_temp", "qualified_name": "set_temp", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["contextmanager"], "docstring": "Sets this item to a specified value only inside a with block.\n\nUse as::\n\n    ITEM = ConfigItem('ITEM', 'default', 'description')\n\n    with ITEM.set_temp('newval'):\n        #... do something that wants ITEM's value to be 'newval' ...\n        print(ITEM)\n\n    # ITEM is now 'default' after the with blo", "start_line": 343, "end_line": 368, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload", "qualified_name": "reload", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reloads the value of this ``ConfigItem`` from the relevant\nconfiguration file.\n\nReturns\n-------\nval : object\n    The new value loaded from the configuration file.", "start_line": 370, "end_line": 397, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 399, "end_line": 403, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 405, "end_line": 415, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the value of this ``ConfigItem``.\n\nReturns\n-------\nval : object\n    This item's value, with a type determined by the ``cfgtype``\n    attribute.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If the configuration value as stored is not this item's type.", "start_line": 417, "end_line": 486, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_validate_val", "qualified_name": "_validate_val", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Validates the provided value based on cfgtype and returns the\ntype-cast value.\n\nthrows the underlying configobj exception if it fails", "start_line": 488, "end_line": 497, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "section_name", "qualified_name": "section_name", "args": ["section"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 433, "end_line": 437, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "InvalidConfigurationItemWarning", "bases": ["AstropyWarning"], "methods": [], "docstring": "A Warning that is issued when the configuration value specified in the\nastropy configuration file does not match the type expected for that\nconfiguration value.", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 47}, {"name": "ConfigurationMissingWarning", "bases": ["AstropyWarning"], "methods": [], "docstring": "A Warning that is issued when the configuration directory cannot be\naccessed (usually due to a permissions problem). If this warning appears,\nconfiguration items will be set to their defaults rather than read from the\nconfiguration file, and no configuration will persist across sessions.", "start_line": 53, "end_line": 58}, {"name": "ConfigurationDefaultMissingError", "bases": ["ValueError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "An exception that is raised when the configuration defaults (which\nshould be generated at build-time) are missing.", "start_line": 62, "end_line": 65}, {"name": "ConfigurationDefaultMissingWarning", "bases": ["AstropyWarning"], "methods": [], "docstring": "A warning that is issued when the configuration defaults (which\nshould be generated at build-time) are missing.", "start_line": 69, "end_line": 72}, {"name": "ConfigurationChangedWarning", "bases": ["AstropyWarning"], "methods": [], "docstring": "A warning that the configuration options have changed.", "start_line": 75, "end_line": 78}, {"name": "_ConfigNamespaceMeta", "bases": ["type"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 81, "end_line": 88}, {"name": "ConfigNamespace", "bases": [], "methods": ["__iter__", "values", "items", "set_temp", "reload", "reset"], "docstring": "A namespace of configuration items.  Each subpackage with\nconfiguration items should define a subclass of this class,\ncontaining `ConfigItem` instances as members.\n\nFor example::\n\n    class Conf(_config.ConfigNamespace):\n        unicode_output = _config.ConfigItem(\n            False,\n            'Us", "start_line": 91, "end_line": 190}, {"name": "ConfigItem", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__set__", "__get__", "set", "set_temp", "reload", "__repr__", "__str__", "__call__", "_validate_val"], "docstring": "A setting and associated value stored in a configuration file.\n\nThese objects should be created as members of\n`ConfigNamespace` subclasses, for example::\n\n    class _Conf(config.ConfigNamespace):\n        unicode_output = config.ConfigItem(\n            False,\n            'Use Unicode characters when ", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 497}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module contains classes and functions to standardize access to\nconfiguration files for Astropy and affiliated packages.\n\n.. note::\n    The configuration system makes use of the 'configobj' package, which stores\n    configuration in a text format like that used in the standard library\n    `ConfigParser`. More information and documentation for configobj can be\n    found at https://configobj.readthedocs.io .", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/table/bst.py", "file_hash": "66dc43b7328a5ae239eafe443d463af8c641280cd510cf37160c8600fb0996f1", "imports": [{"module": "operator", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "__gt__", "qualified_name": "__gt__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 14, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__ge__", "qualified_name": "__ge__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 17, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__lt__", "qualified_name