on to allow use as a mixin column.\n\nReturns the shape of the first item that has a shape at all,\nor ``()`` if none of the values has a shape attribute.", "start_line": 101, "end_line": 109, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_column", "qualified_name": "add_column", "args": ["self", "col", "index"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 359, "end_line": 364, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "colnames", "qualified_name": "colnames", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 367, "end_line": 368, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "itercols", "qualified_name": "itercols", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 370, "end_line": 371, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "SerializedColumnInfo", "bases": ["MixinInfo"], "methods": ["_represent_as_dict"], "docstring": "Minimal info to allow SerializedColumn to be recognized as a mixin Column.\n\nUsed to help create a dict of columns in ColumnInfo for structured data.", "start_line": 77, "end_line": 86}, {"name": "SerializedColumn", "bases": ["dict"], "methods": ["shape"], "docstring": "Subclass of dict used to serialize  mixin columns.\n\nIt is used in the representation to contain the name and possible\nother info for a mixin column or attribute (either primary data or an\narray-like attribute) that is serialized as a column in the table.", "start_line": 89, "end_line": 109}, {"name": "_TableLite", "bases": ["OrderedDict"], "methods": ["add_column", "colnames", "itercols"], "docstring": "Minimal table-like object for _construct_mixin_from_columns.  This allows\nmanipulating the object like a Table but without the actual overhead\nfor a full Table.\n\nMore pressing, there is an issue with constructing MaskedColumn, where the\nencoded Column components (data, mask) are turned into a Masked", "start_line": 347, "end_line": 371}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error