clusive with respect to the endpoints. The first\n    argument x correspond", "start_line": 301, "end_line": 317, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "replace", "qualified_name": "replace", "args": ["self", "row", "col_name", "val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Replace the value of a column at a given position.\n\nParameters\n----------\nrow : int\n    Row number to modify\ncol_name : str\n    Name of the Column to modify\nval : col.info.dtype\n    Value to insert at specified row of col", "start_line": 319, "end_line": 335, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "replace_rows", "qualified_name": "replace_rows", "args": ["self", "col_slice"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Modify rows in this index to agree with the specified\nslice. For example, given an index\n{'5': 1, '2': 0, '3': 2} on a column ['2', '5', '3'],\nan input col_slice of [2, 0] will result in the relabeling\n{'3': 0, '2': 1} on the sliced column ['3', '2'].\n\nParameters\n----------\ncol_slice : list\n    Indi", "start_line": 337, "end_line": 351, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sort", "qualified_name": "sort", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make row numbers follow the same sort order as the keys\nof the index.", "start_line": 353, "end_line": 358, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sorted_data", "qualified_name": "sorted_data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a list of rows in sorted order based on keys;\nessentially acts as an argsort() on columns.", "start_line": 360, "end_line": 365, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a sliced version of this index.\n\nParameters\n----------\nitem : slice\n    Input slice\n\nReturns\n-------\nSlicedIndex\n    A sliced reference to this index.", "start_line": 367, "end_line": 381, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__r