": "Restore the internal state of the Column/MaskedColumn for pickling\npurposes.  This requires that the last element of ``state`` is a\n5-tuple that has Column-specific state values.", "start_line": 651, "end_line": 675, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a 3-tuple for pickling a Column.  Use the super-class\nfunctionality but then add in a 5-tuple of Column-specific values\nthat get used in __setstate__.", "start_line": 677, "end_line": 697, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_finalize__", "qualified_name": "__array_finalize__", "args": ["self", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 699, "end_line": 715, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_wrap__", "qualified_name": "__array_wrap__", "args": ["self", "out_arr", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "__array_wrap__ is called at the end of every ufunc.\n\nNormally, we want a Column object back and do not have to do anything\nspecial. But there are two exceptions:\n\n1) If the output shape is different (e.g. for reduction ufuncs\n   like sum() or mean()), a Column still linking to a parent_table\n   make", "start_line": 717, "end_line": 744, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The name of this column.", "start_line": 747, "end_line": 751, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": ["name.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 754, "end_line": 762, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "format", "qualified_name": "format", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Format string for displaying values in this column.", "start_line": 765, "end_line": 769, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "format", "qualified_name": "format", "args": ["self", "format_string"], "decorators": ["format.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 772, "end_line": 786, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "descr", "qualified_name": "descr", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Array-interface compliant full description of the column.\n\nThis returns a 3-tuple (name, type, shape) that can always be\nused in a structured array dtype definition.", "start_line": 789, "end_line": 795, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "iter_str_vals", "qualified_name": "iter_str_vals", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an iterator that yields the string-formatted values of this\ncolumn.\n\nReturns\n-------\nstr_vals : iterator\n    Column values formatted as strings", "start_line": 797, "end_line": 812, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "attrs_equal", "qualified_name": "attrs_equal", "args": ["self", "col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compare the column attributes of ``col`` to this object.\n\nThe comparison attributes are: ``name``, ``unit``, ``dtype``,\n``format``, ``description``, and ``meta``.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncol : Column\n    Comparison column\n\nReturns\n-------\nequal : bool\n    True if all attributes are equal", "start_line": 814, "end_line": 836, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_formatter", "qualified_name": "_formatter", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 839, "end_line": 840, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pformat", "qualified_name": "pformat", "args": ["self", "max_lines", "show_name", "show_unit", "show_dtype", "html"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of formatted string representation of column values.\n\nIf no value of ``max_lines`` is supplied then the height of the\nscreen terminal is used to set ``max_lines``.  If the terminal\nheight cannot be determined then the default will be\ndetermined using the ``astropy.conf.max_lines`` conf", "start_line": 842, "end_line": 891, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pprint", "qualified_name": "pprint", "args": ["self", "max_lines", "show_name", "show_unit", "show_dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Print a formatted string representation of column values.\n\nIf no value of ``max_lines`` is supplied then the height of the\nscreen terminal is used to set ``max_lines``.  If the terminal\nheight cannot be determined then the default will be\ndetermined using the ``astropy.conf.max_lines`` configuration", "start_line": 893, "end_line": 931, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "more", "qualified_name": "more", "args": ["self", "max_lines", "show_name", "show_unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Interactively browse column with a paging interface.\n\nSupported keys::\n\n  f, <space> : forward one page\n  b : back one page\n  r : refresh same page\n  n : next row\n  p : previous row\n  < : go to beginning\n  > : go to end\n  q : quit browsing\n  h : print this help\n\nParameters\n----------\nmax_lines : int", "start_line": 933, "end_line": 963, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The unit associated with this column.  May be a string or a\n`astropy.units.UnitBase` instance.\n\nSetting the ``unit`` property does not change the values of the\ndata.  To perform a unit conversion, use ``convert_unit_to``.", "start_line": 966, "end_line": 974, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": ["unit.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 977, "end_line": 981, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["unit.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 984, "end_line": 985, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "searchsorted", "qualified_name": "searchsorted", "args": ["self", "v", "side", "sorter"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 987, "end_line": 996, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convert_unit_to", "qualified_name": "convert_unit_to", "args": ["self", "new_unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Converts the values of the column in-place from the current\nunit to the given unit.\n\nTo change the unit associated with this column without\nactually changing the data values, simply set the ``unit``\nproperty.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnew_unit : str or `astropy.units.UnitBase` instance\n    The unit to ", "start_line": 1000, "end_line": 1026, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "groups", "qualified_name": "groups", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1029, "end_line": 1032, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "group_by", "qualified_name": "group_by", "args": ["self", "keys"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Group this column by the specified ``keys``.\n\nThis effectively splits the column into groups which correspond to\nunique values of the ``keys`` grouping object.  The output is a new\n`Column` or `MaskedColumn` which contains a copy of this column but\nsorted by row according to ``keys``.\n\nThe ``keys`` ", "start_line": 1034, "end_line": 1056, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_copy_groups", "qualified_name": "_copy_groups", "args": ["self", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Copy current groups into a copy of self ``out``.", "start_line": 1058, "end_line": 1068, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1073, "end_line": 1074, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "quantity", "qualified_name": "quantity", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A view of this table column as a `~astropy.units.Quantity` object with\nunits 