\nonto the finer grid ``obstime``.", "start_line": 316, "end_line": 327, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "apco", "qualified_name": "apco", "args": ["self", "frame_or_coord"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrapper for ``erfa.apco``, used in conversions AltAz <-> ICRS and CIRS <-> ICRS.\n\nParameters\n----------\nframe_or_coord : ``astropy.coordinates.BaseCoordinateFrame`` or ``astropy.coordinates.SkyCoord``\n    Frame or coordinate instance in the corresponding frame\n    for which to calculate the calculat", "start_line": 329, "end_line": 386, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "apcs", "qualified_name": "apcs", "args": ["self", "frame_or_coord"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrapper for ``erfa.apci``, used in conversions GCRS <-> ICRS.\n\nParameters\n----------\nframe_or_coord : ``astropy.coordinates.BaseCoordinateFrame`` or ``astropy.coordinates.SkyCoord``\n    Frame or coordinate instance in the corresponding frame\n    for which to calculate the calculate the astrom values", "start_line": 388, "end_line": 413, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate", "qualified_name": "validate", "args": ["cls", "value"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 425, "end_line": 428, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "ErfaAstrom", "bases": [], "methods": ["apco", "apcs", "apio"], "docstring": "The default provider for astrometry values.\nA utility class to extract the necessary arguments for\nerfa functions from frame attributes, call the corresponding\nerfa functions and return the astrom object.", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 185}, {"name": "ErfaAstromInterpolator", "bases": ["ErfaAstrom"], "methods": ["__init__", "_get_support_points", "_prepare_earth_position_vel", "_get_c2i", "_get_cip", "_get_polar_motion", "apco", "apcs"], "docstring": "A provider for astrometry values that does not call erfa\nfor each individual timestamp but interpolates linearly\nbetween support poi