s\n----------\ndata : `~astropy.coordinates.BaseRepresentation`\n    The representation to use as the data for the new frame.\n**kwargs\n    Any a", "start_line": 1018, "end_line": 1039, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "represent_as", "qualified_name": "represent_as", "args": ["self", "base", "s", "in_frame_units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate and return a new representation of this frame's `data`\nas a Representation object.\n\nNote: In order to make an in-place change of the representation\nof a Frame or SkyCoord object, set the ``representation``\nattribute of that object to the desired new representation, or\nuse the ``set_represen", "start_line": 1041, "end_line": 1237, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "transform_to", "qualified_name": "transform_to", "args": ["self", "new_frame"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Transform this object's coordinate data to a new frame.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnew_frame : coordinate-like or `~astropy.coordinates.BaseCoordinateFrame` subclass instance\n    The frame to transform this coordinate frame into.\n    The frame class option is deprecated.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntransframe : co", "start_line": 1239, "end_line": 1302, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_transformable_to", "qualified_name": "is_transformable_to", "args": ["self", "new_frame"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines if this coordinate frame can be transformed to another\ngiven frame.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnew_frame : `~astropy.coordinates.BaseCoordinateFrame` subclass or instance\n    The proposed frame to transform into.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntransformable : bool or str\n    `True` if this can be transform", "start_line": 1304, "end_line": 1345, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_frame_attr_default", "qualified_name": "is_frame_attr_default", "args": ["self", "attrnm"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determine whether or not a frame attribute has its value because it's\nthe default value, or because this frame was created with that value\nexplicitly requested.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattrnm : str\n    The name of the attribute to check.\n\nReturns\n-------\nisdefault : bool\n    True if the attribute ``a", "start_line": 1347, "end_line": 1364, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_frameattr_equiv", "qualified_name": "_frameattr_equiv", "args": ["left_fattr", "right_fattr"], "decorators": ["staticmethod"], "docstring": "Determine if two frame attributes are equivalent.  Implemented as a\nstaticmethod mainly as a convenient location, although conceivable it\nmight be desirable for subclasses to override this behavior.\n\nPrimary purpose is to check for equality of representations.  This\naspect can actually be simplified", "start_line": 1367, "end_line": 1431, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_equivalent_frame", "qualified_name": "is_equivalent_frame", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Checks if this object is the same frame as the ``other`` object.\n\nTo be the same frame, two objects must be the same frame class and have\nthe same frame attributes.  Note that it does *not* matter what, if any,\ndata either object has.\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : :class:`~astropy.coordinates.BaseC", "start_line": 1433, "end_line": 1468, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1470, "end_line": 1480, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_data_repr", "qualified_name": "_data_repr", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a string representation of the coordinate data.", "start_line": 1482, "end_line": 1556, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_frame_attrs_repr", "qualified_name": "_frame_attrs_repr", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a string representation of the frame's attributes, if any.", "star