.json and parse them into\na SiteRegistry.", "start_line": 129, "end_line": 135, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_downloaded_sites", "qualified_name": "get_downloaded_sites", "args": ["jsonurl"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Load observatory database from data.astropy.org and parse into a SiteRegistry.", "start_line": 138, "end_line": 150, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 35, "end_line": 39, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "site_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns an EarthLocation for a known site in this registry.\n\nParameters\n----------\nsite_name : str\n    Name of the observatory (case-insensitive).\n\nReturns\n-------\nsite : `~astropy.coordinates.EarthLocation`\n    The location of the observatory.", "start_line": 41, "end_line": 66, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__len__", "qualified_name": "__len__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 68, "end_line": 69, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 71, "end_line": 72, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__contains__", "qualified_name": "__contains__", "args": ["self", "site_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 74, "end_line": 75, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "names", "qualified_name": "names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The names in this registry.  Note that these are *not* exactly the same\nas the keys: keys are always lower-case, while `names` is what you\nshould use for the actual readable names (which may be case-sensitive).\n\nReturns\n-------\nsite : list of str\n    The names of the sites in this registry", "start_