roduce artifacts when applied repeatedly to the same data.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nBy default the Box kernel uses the ``linear_interp`` discretization mo", "start_line": 183, "end_line": 247}, {"name": "Box2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Box filter kernel.\n\nThe Box filter or running mean is a smoothing filter. It is not isotropic\nand can produce artifacts when applied repeatedly to the same data.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nBy default the Box kernel uses the ``linear_interp`` discretization mo", "start_line": 250, "end_line": 317}, {"name": "Tophat2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Tophat filter kernel.\n\nThe Tophat filter is an isotropic smoothing filter. It can produce\nartifacts when applied repeatedly on the same data.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius : int\n    Radius of the filter kernel.\nmode : {'center', 'lin", "start_line": 320, "end_line": 376}, {"name": "Ring2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Ring filter kernel.\n\nThe Ring filter kernel is the difference between two Tophat kernels of\ndifferent width. This kernel is useful for, e.g., background estimation.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius_in : number\n    Inner radius of the ri", "start_line": 379, "end_line": 440}, {"name": "Trapezoid1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "1D trapezoid kernel.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwidth : number\n    Width of the filter kernel, defined as the width of the constant part,\n    before it begins to slope down.\nslope : number\n    Slope of the filter kernel's tails\nmode : {'cen", "start_line": 443, "end_line": 500}, {"name": "TrapezoidDisk2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D trapezoid kernel.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius : number\n    Width of the filter kernel, defined as the width of the constant part,\n    before it begins to slope down.\nslope : number\n    Slope of the filter kernel's tails\nmode : {'ce", "start_line": 503, "end_line": 561}, {"name": "RickerWavelet1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "1D Ricker wavelet filter kernel (sometimes known as a \"Mexican Hat\"\nkernel).\n\nThe Ricker wavelet, or inverted Gaussian-Laplace filter, is a\nbandpass filter. It smooths the data and removes slowly varying\nor constant structures (e.g. Background). It is useful for peak or\nmulti-scale detection.\n\nThis ", "start_line": 564, "end_line": 635}, {"name": "RickerWavelet2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Ricker wavelet filter kernel (sometimes known as a \"Mexican Hat\"\nkernel).\n\nThe Ricker wavelet, or inverted Gaussian-Laplace filter, is a\nbandpass filter. It smooths the data and removes slowly varying\nor constant structures (e.g. Background). It is useful for peak or\nmulti-scale detection.\n\nThis ", "start_line": 638, "end_line": 713}, {"name": "AiryDisk2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Airy disk kernel.\n\nThis kernel models the diffraction pattern of a circular aperture.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius : float\n    The radius of the Airy disk kernel (radius of the first zero).\nx_size : int, optional\n    Size in x direc", "start_line": 716, "end_line": 777}, {"name": "Moffat2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Moffat kernel.\n\nThis kernel is a typical model for a seeing limited PSF.\n\nThe generated kernel is normalized so that it integrates to 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\ngamma : float\n    Core width of the Moffat model.\nalpha : float\n    Power index of the Moffat model.\nx_size : int, optional\n    Size in x", "start_line": 780, "end_line": 846}, {"name": "Model1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Create kernel from 1D model.\n\nThe model has to be centered on x = 0.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.Fittable1DModel`\n    Kernel response function model\nx_size : int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = \u230a8*width +1\u230b.\n    Must be odd.\nmode : {'center', 'l", "start_line": 849, "end_line": 912}, {"name": "Model2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Create kernel from 2D model.\n\nThe model has to be centered on x = 0 and y = 0.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.Fittable2DModel`\n    Kernel response function model\nx_size : int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = \u230a8*width +1\u230b.\n    Must be odd.\ny_size : i", "start_line": 915, "end_line": 981}, {"name": "CustomKernel", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__", "array", "array"], "docstring": "Create filter kernel from list or array.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : list or array\n    Filter kernel array. Size must be odd.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If array is not a list or array.\n`~astropy.convolution.KernelSizeError`\n    If array size is even.\n\nSee Also\n--------\nModel2DKernel, Model1DKe", "start_line": 984, "end_line": 1053}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/convolution/core.py", "file_hash": "6dafe0e2d2907b3369dee2efa26a3dcf2aae4861239242a5a33e464ae866f035", "imports": [{"module": "copy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy.utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["KernelArithmeticError", "add_kernel_arrays_1D", "add_kernel_arrays_2D", "discretize_model"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "kernel_arithmetics", "qualified_name": "kernel_arithmetics", "args": ["kernel", "value", "operation"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add, subtract or multiply two kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nkernel : `astropy.convolution.Kernel`\n    Kernel instance.\nvalue : `astropy.convolution.Kernel`, float, or int\n    Value to operate with.\noperation : {'add', 'sub', 'mul'}\n    One of the following operations:\n        * 'add'\n            A", "start_line": 329, "end_line": 386, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 51, "end_line": 52, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "truncation", "qualified_name": "truncation", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Absolute deviation of the sum of the kernel array values from\none.", "start_line": 55, "end_line": 60, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_bool", "qualified_name": "is_bool", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Indicates if kernel is bool.\n\nIf the kernel is bool the multiplication in the convolution could\nbe omitted, to increase the performance.", "start_line": 63, "end_line": 70, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "model", "qualified_name": "model", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Kernel response model.", "start_line": 73, "end_line": 77, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dimension", "qualified_name": "dimension", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Kernel dimension.", "start_line": 80, "end_line": 84, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "center", "qualified_name": "center", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Index of the kernel center.", "start_line": 87, "end_line": 91, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "normalize", "qualified_name": "normalize", "args": ["self", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Normalize the filter kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmode : {'integral', 'peak'}\n    One of the following modes:\n        * 'integral' (default)\n            Kernel is normalized such that its integral = 1.\n        * 'peak'\n            Kernel is normalized such that its peak = 1.", "start_line": 93, "end_line": 122, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Shape of the kernel array.", "start_line": 125, "end_line": 129, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "separable", "qualified_name": "separable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Indicates if the filter kernel is separable.\n\nA 2D filter is separable, when its filter array can be written as the\nouter product of two 1D arrays.\n\nIf a filter kernel is separable, higher dimension convolutions will be\nperformed by applying the 1D filter array consecutively on every dimension.\nThis", "start_line": 132, "end_line": 144, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "array", "qualified_name": "array", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Filter kernel array.", "start_line": 147, "end_line": 151, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__add__", "qualified_name": "__add__", "args": ["self", "kernel"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add two filter kernels.", "start_line": 153, "end_line": 157, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__sub__", "qualified_name": "__sub__", "args": ["self", "kernel"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Subtract two filter kernels.", "start_line": 159, "end_line": 163, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__mul__", "qualified_name": "__mul__", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Multiply kernel with number or convolve two kernels.", "start_line": 165, "end_line": 169, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__rmul__", "qualified_name": "__rmul__", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Multiply kernel with number or convolve two kernels.", "start_line": 171, "end_line": 175, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array__", "qualified_name": "__array__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Array representation of the kernel.", "start_line": 177, "end_line": 181, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_wrap__", "qualified_name": "__array_wrap__", "args": ["self", "array", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrapper for multiplication with numpy arrays.", "start_line": 183, "end_line": 190, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "model", "x_size", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 226, "end_line": 252, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "model", "x_size", "y_size", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 291, "end_line": 326, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Kernel", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "truncation", "is_bool", "model", "dimension", "center", "normalize", "shape", "separable", "array", "__add__", "__sub__", "__mul__", "__rmul__", "__array__", "__array_wrap__"], "docstring": "Convolution kernel base class.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : ndarray\n    Kernel array.", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 190}, {"name": "Kernel1D", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Base class for 1D filter kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.FittableModel`\n    Model to be evaluated.\nx_size : int or None, optional\n    Size of the kernel array. Default = \u230a8*width+1\u230b.\n    Only used if ``array`` is None.\narray : ndarray or None, optional\n    Kernel array.\nwi", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 252}, {"name": "Kernel2D", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Base class for 2D filter kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.FittableModel`\n    Model to be evaluated.\nx_size : int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = \u230a8*width + 1\u230b.\n    Only used if ``array`` is None.\ny_size : int, optional\n    Size in y directio", "start_line": 255, "end_line": 326}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module contains the convolution and filter functionalities of astropy.\n\nA few conceptual notes:\nA filter kernel is mainly characterized by its response function. In the 1D\ncase we speak of \"impulse response function\", in the 2D case we call it \"point\nspread function\". This response function is given for every kernel by an\nastropy `FittableModel`, which is evaluated on a grid to obtain a filter array,\nwhich can then be applied to binned data.\n\nThe model is centered on the array and should have an amplitude such that the array\nintegrates to one per default.\n\nCurrently only symmetric 2D kernels are supported.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/convolution/convolve.py", "file_hash": "b01b23ef161d616dabe7d8567fecc757e87168fd41449710228cfb7548e0aa57", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "functools", "names": ["partial"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.modeling.convolution", "names": ["Convolution"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.modeling.core", "names": ["SPECIAL_OPERATORS", "CompoundModel"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.nddata", "names": ["support_nddata"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.console", "names": ["human_file_size"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "_convolve", "names": ["_convolveNd_c"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["MAX_NORMALIZATION", "Kernel", "Kernel1D", "Kernel2D"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["KernelSizeError", "has_even_axis"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.fft", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "_next_fast_lengths", "qualified_name": "_next_fast_lengths", "args": ["shape"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Find optimal or good sizes to pad an array of ``shape`` to for better\nperformance with `numpy.fft.*fft` and `scipy.fft.*fft`.\nCalculated directly with `scipy.fft.next_fast_len`, if available; otherwise\nlooked up from list and scaled by powers of 10, if necessary.", "start_line": 50, "end_line": 76, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_copy_input_if_needed", "qualified_name": "_copy_input_if_needed", "args": ["input", "dtype", "order", "nan_treatment", "mask", "fill_value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 79, "end_line": 127, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve", "qualified_name": "convolve", "args": ["array", "kernel", "boundary", "fill_value", "nan_treatment", "normalize_kernel", "mask", "preserve_nan", "normalization_zero_tol"], "decorators": ["support_nddata(data='array')"], "docstring": "Convolve an array with a kernel.\n\nThis routine differs from `scipy.ndimage.convolve` because\nit includes a special treatment for ``NaN`` values. Rather than\nincluding ``NaN`` values in the array in the convolution calculation, which\ncauses large ``NaN`` holes in the convolved array, ``NaN`` values a", "start_line": 131, "end_line": 464, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve_fft", "qualified_name": "convolve_fft", "args": ["array", "kernel", "boundary", "fill_value", "nan_treatment", "normalize_kernel", "normalization_zero_tol", "preserve_nan", "mask", "crop", "return_fft", "fft_pad", "psf_pad", "min_wt", "allow_huge", "fftn", "ifftn", "complex_dtype", "dealias"], "decorators": ["support_nddata(data='array')"], "docstring": "Convolve an ndarray with an nd-kernel.  Returns a convolved image with\n``shape = array.shape``.  Assumes kernel is centered.\n\n`convolve_fft` is very similar to `convolve` in that it replaces ``NaN``\nvalues in the original image with interpolated values using the kernel as\nan interpolation function. ", "start_line": 468, "end_line": 951, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "interpolate_replace_nans", "qualified_name": "interpolate_replace_nans", "args": ["array", "kernel", "convolve"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a data set containing NaNs, replace the NaNs by interpolating from\nneighboring data points with a given kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : `numpy.ndarray`\n    Array to be convolved with ``kernel``.  It can be of any\n    dimensionality, though only 1, 2, and 3d arrays have been tested.\nkern", "start_line": 954, "end_line": 997, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve_models", "qualified_name": "convolve_models", "args": ["model", "kernel", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convolve two models using `~astropy.convolution.convolve_fft`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Functional model\nkernel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Convolution kernel\nmode : str\n    Keyword representing which function to use for convolution.\n        * 'convo", "start_line": 1000, "end_line": 1032, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve_models_fft", "qualified_name": "convolve_models_fft", "args": ["model", "kernel", "bounding_box", "resolution", "cache"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convolve two models using `~astropy.convolution.convolve_fft`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Functional model\nkernel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Convolution kernel\nbounding_box : tuple\n    The bounding box which encompasses enough of the support of both\n ", "start_line": 1035, "end_line": 1066, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/__init__.py", "file_hash": "a968b26d0a0e06991f74d359255af0ac35715ce2d2a152ce4cbe0de5fd4c0c5c", "imports": [], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This subpackage contains modules and packages for interpreting data storage\nformats used by and in astropy.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/utils/data.py", "file_hash": "b2f939614fac52acb7b3b98dc70c94f61cfe02d15acab7486239b25d610c8513", "imports": [{"module": "atexit", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "contextlib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "errno", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "fnmatch", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "ftplib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "functools", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hashlib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "io", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "os", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "re", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "shutil", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "urllib.error", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "urllib.parse", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "urllib.request", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "zipfile", "names": [], "is_from": false, "ali