gister"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1756, "end_line": 1775, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_download_cache", "qualified_name": "clear_download_cache", "args": ["hashorurl", "pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clears the data file cache by deleting the local file(s).\n\nIf a URL is provided, it will be the name used in the cache. The contents\nmay have been downloaded from this URL or from a mirror or they may have\nbeen provided by the user. See `~download_file` for details.\n\nFor the purposes of this functio", "start_line": 1778, "end_line": 1845, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_download_cache_loc", "qualified_name": "_get_download_cache_loc", "args": ["pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Finds the path to the cache directory and makes them if they don't exist.\n\nParameters\n----------\npkgname : `str`, optional\n    The package name to use to locate the download cache. i.e. for\n    ``pkgname='astropy'`` the default cache location is\n    ``~/.astropy/cache``.\n\nReturns\n-------\ndatadir : s", "start_line": 1848, "end_line": 1882, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_url_to_dirname", "qualified_name": "_url_to_dirname", "args": ["url"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1885, "end_line": 1895, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_download_cache", "qualified_name": "check_download_cache", "args": ["pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Do a consistency check on the cache.\n\n.. note::\n\n    Since v5.0, this function no longer returns anything.\n\nBecause the cache is shared by all versions of ``astropy`` in all virtualenvs\nrun by your user, possibly concurrently, it could accumulate problems.\nThis could lead to hard-to-debug problems o", "start_line": 1918, "end_line": 2006, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_SafeTemporaryDirectory", "qualified_name": "_SafeTemporaryDirectory", "args": ["suffix", "prefix", "dir"], "decorators": ["contextlib.contextmanager"], "docstring": "Temporary directory context manager.\n\nThis will not raise an exception if the temporary directory goes away\nbefore it's supposed to be deleted. Specifically, what is deleted will\nbe the directory *name* produced; if no such directory exists, no\nexception will be raised.\n\nIt would be safer to delete ", "start_line": 2010, "end_line": 2032, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_rmtree", "qualified_name": "_rmtree", "args": ["path", "replace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "More-atomic rmtree. Ignores missing directory.", "start_line": 2035, "end_line": 2074, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "import_file_to_cache", "qualified_name": "import_file_to_cache", "args": ["url_key", "filename", "remove_original", "pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Import the on-disk file specified by filename to the cache.\n\nThe provided ``url_key`` will be the name used in the cache. The file\nshould contain the contents of this URL, at least notionally (the URL may\nbe temporarily or permanently unavailable). It is using ``url_key`` that\nusers will request the", "start_line": 2077, "end_line": 2139, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_cached_urls", "qualified_name": "get_cached_urls", "args": ["pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the list of URLs in the cache. Especially useful for looking up what\nfiles are stored in your cache when you don't have internet access.\n\nThe listed URLs are the keys programs should use to access the file\ncontents, but those contents may have actually been obtained from a mirror.\nSee `~download", "start_line": 2142, "end_line": 2167, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cache_contents", "qualified_name": "cache_contents", "args": ["pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Obtain a dict mapping cached URLs to filenames.\n\nThis dictionary is a read-only snapshot of the state of the cache when this\nfunction was called. If other processes are actively working with the\ncache, it is possible for them to delete files that are listed in this\ndictionary. Use with some caution ", "start_line": 2170, "end_line": 2192, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "export_download_cache", "qualified_name": "export_download_cache", "args": ["filename_or_obj", "urls", "overwrite", "pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Exports the cache contents as a ZIP file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename_or_obj : str or file-like\n    Where to put the created ZIP file. Must be something the zipfile\n    module can write to.\nurls : iterable of str or None\n    The URLs to include in the exported cache. The default is all\n    URLs ", "start_line": 2195, "end_line": 2232, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "import_download_cache", "qualified_name": "import_download_cache", "args": ["filename_or_obj", "urls", "update_cache", "pkgname"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Imports the contents of a ZIP file into the cache.\n\nEach member of the ZIP file should be named by a quoted version of the\nURL whose contents it stores. These names are decoded with\n:func:`~urllib.parse.unquote`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename_or_obj : str or file-like\n    Where the stored ZIP file", "start_line": 2235, "end_line": 2285, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__del__", "qualified_name": "__del__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 75, "end_line": 81, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__del__", "qualified_name": "__del__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 85, "end_line": 91, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "init", "qualified_name": "init", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1119, "end_line": 1126, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "connect_ftp", "qualified_name": "connect_ftp", "args": ["self", "user", "passwd", "host", "port", "dirs", 