l code), use the private\nname for the attribute by prepending an underscore\n(i.e. ``self._name``), or set an alternative explicitl", "start_line": 232, "end_line": 319, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deprecated_renamed_argument", "qualified_name": "deprecated_renamed_argument", "args": ["old_name", "new_name", "since", "arg_in_kwargs", "relax", "pending", "warning_type", "alternative", "message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Deprecate a _renamed_ or _removed_ function argument.\n\nThe decorator assumes that the argument with the ``old_name`` was removed\nfrom the function signature and the ``new_name`` replaced it at the\n**same position** in the signature.  If the ``old_name`` argument is\ngiven when calling the decorated f", "start_line": 322, "end_line": 608, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "format_doc", "qualified_name": "format_doc", "args": ["docstring"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Replaces the docstring of the decorated object and then formats it.\n\nThe formatting works like :meth:`str.format` and if the decorated object\nalready has a docstring this docstring can be included in the new\ndocumentation if you use the ``{__doc__}`` placeholder.\nIts primary use is for reusing a *lo", "start_line": 929, "end_line": 1151, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deprecate_doc", "qualified_name": "deprecate_doc", "args": ["old_doc", "message"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a given docstring with a deprecation message prepended\nto it.", "start_line": 90, "end_line": 103, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_function", "qualified_name": "get_function", "args": ["func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a function or classmethod (or other function wrapper type), get\nthe function object.", "start_line": 105, "end_line": 112, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deprecate_function", "qualified_name": "deprecate_function", "args": ["func", "message", "warning_type"],