It may be used to calculate\nthe proper distance between two redshifts, e.g. for the mean free path\nto ionizing radiation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or", "start_line": 995, "end_line": 1012, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "age", "qualified_name": "age", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Age of the universe in Gyr at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nt : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['time']\n    The age of the universe in Gyr at each input redshift.\n\nSee Also\n--------\nz_at_value :", "start_line": 1014, "end_line": 1031, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_age", "qualified_name": "_age", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Age of the universe in Gyr at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis internal function exists to be re-defined for optimizations.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nt : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['time']\n    The age of the univ", "start_line": 1033, "end_line": 1048, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_integral_age", "qualified_name": "_integral_age", "args": [], "decorators": ["vectorize_redshift_method"], "docstring": "Age of the universe at redshift ``z``. Value in units of Hubble time.\n\nCalculated using explicit integration.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nt : float or ndarray\n    The age of the universe at each input re", "start_line": 1051, "end_line": 1071, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "critical_density", "qualified_name": "critical_density", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Critical density in grams per cubic cm at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nrho : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Critical density in g/cm^3 at each input redshift.", "start_line": 1073, "end_line": 1086, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_distance", "qualified_name": "comoving_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance in Mpc at a given redshift.\n\nThe comoving distance along the line-of-sight between two objects\nremains constant with time for objects in the Hubble flow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nRetur", "start_line": 1088, "end_line": 1104, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance in Mpc between objects at redshifts\n``z1`` and ``z2``.\n\nThe comoving distance along the line-of-sight between two objects\nremains constant with time for objects in the Hubble flow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Nu", "start_line": 1106, "end_line": 1124, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2_scalar", "qualified_name": "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2_scalar", "args": [], "decorators": ["vectorize_redshift_method(nin=2)"], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance between objects at redshifts ``z1`` and\n``z2``. Value in Mpc.\n\nThe comoving distance along the line-of-sight between two objects\nremains constant with time for objects in the Hubble flow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~num", "start_line": 1127, "end_line": 1146, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance in Mpc between objects at redshifts\n``z1`` and ``z2``. The comoving distance along the line-of-sight\nbetween two objects remains constant with time for objects in the\nHubble flow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : Quantity-like ['redshift'] or array-like\n    Input redsh", "start_line": 1148, "end_line": 1165, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_transverse_distance", "qualified_name": "comoving_transverse_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving transverse distance in Mpc at a given redshift.\n\nThis value is the transverse comoving distance at redshift ``z``\ncorresponding to an angular separation of 1 radian. This is the same as\nthe comoving distance if :math:`\\Omega_k` is zero (as in the current\nconcordance Lambda-CDM model).\n\nPara", "start_line": 1167, "end_line": 1189, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_comoving_transverse_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "_comoving_transverse_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving transverse distance in Mpc between two redshifts.\n\nThis value is the transverse comoving distance at redshift ``z2`` as\nseen from redshift ``z1`` corresponding to an angular separation of\n1 radian. This is the same as the comoving distance if :math:`\\Omega_k`\nis zero (as in the current conc", "start_line": 1191, "end_line": 1222, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "angular_diameter_distance", "qualified_name": "angular_diameter_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular diameter distance in Mpc at a given redshift.\n\nThis gives the proper (sometimes called 'physical') transverse\ndistance corresponding to an angle of 1 radian for an object\nat redshift ``z`` ([1]_, [2]_, [3]_).\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Num", "start_line": 1224, "end_line": 1248, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "luminosity_distance", "qualified_name": "luminosity_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Luminosity distance in Mpc at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is the distance to use when converting between the bolometric flux\nfrom an object at redshift ``z`` and its bolometric luminosity [1]_.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nRet", "start_line": 1250, "end_line": 1275, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "angular_diameter_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "angular_diameter_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular diameter distance between objects at 2 redshifts.\n\nUseful for gravitational lensing, for example computing the angular\ndiameter distance between a lensed galaxy and the foreground lens.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input red", "start_line": 1277, "end_line": 1304, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "absorption_distance", "qualified_name": "absorption_distance", "args": [], "decorators": ["vectorize_redshift_method"], "docstring": "Absorption distance at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is used to calculate the number of objects with some cross section\nof absorption and number density intersecting a sightline per unit\nredshift path ([1]_, [2]_).\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    I", "start_line": 1307, "end_line": 1331, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "distmod", "qualified_name": "distmod", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Distance modulus at redshift ``z``.\n\nThe distance modulus is defined as the (apparent magnitude - absolute\nmagnitude) for an object at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\ndistmod : `~astropy.unit", "start_line": 1333, "end_line": 1358, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_volume", "qualified_name": "comoving_volume", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving volume in cubic Mpc at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is the volume of the universe encompassed by redshifts less than\n``z``. For the case of :math:`\\Omega_k = 0` it is a sphere of radius\n`comoving_distance` but it is less intuitive if :math:`\\Omega_k` is not.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-lik", "start_line": 1360, "end_line": 1390, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "differential_comoving_volume", "qualified_name": "differential_comoving_volume", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Differential comoving volume at redshift z.\n\nUseful for calculating the effective comoving volume.\nFor example, allows for integration over a comoving volume that has a\nsensitivity function that changes with redshift. The total comoving\nvolume is given by integrating ``differential_comoving_volume``", "start_line": 1392, "end_line": 1413, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "kpc_comoving_per_arcmin", "qualified_name": "kpc_comoving_per_arcmin", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Separation in transverse comoving kpc corresponding to an arcminute at\nredshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['length']\n    The distance in comoving kpc corresponding ", "start_line": 1415, "end_line": 1431, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "kpc_proper_per_arcmin", "qualified_name": "kpc_proper_per_arcmin", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Separation in transverse proper kpc corresponding to an arcminute at\nredshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['length']\n    The distance in proper kpc corresponding to a", "start_line": 1433, "end_line": 1449, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "arcsec_per_kpc_comoving", "qualified_name": "arcsec_per_kpc_comoving", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a comoving kpc at\nredshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntheta : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['angle']\n    The angular separation in arcsec corresponding ", "start_line": 1451, "end_line": 1467, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "arcsec_per_kpc_proper", "qualified_name": "arcsec_per_kpc_proper", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a proper kpc at redshift\n``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntheta : `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['angle']\n    The angular separation in arcsec corresponding to", "start_line": 1469, "end_line": 1485, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init_subclass__", "qualified_name": "__init_subclass__", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1501, "end_line": 1506, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1508, "end_line": 1512, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "nonflat", "qualified_name": "nonflat", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1515, "end_line": 1527, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clone", "qualified_name": "clone", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a copy of this object with updated parameters, as specified.\n\nThis cannot be used to change the type of the cosmology, except for\nchanging to the non-flat version of this cosmology.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmeta : mapping or None (optional, keyword-only)\n    Metadata that will update the curre", "start_line": 1529, "end_line": 1585, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Otot0", "qualified_name": "Otot0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega total; the total density/critical density at z=0.", "start_line": 1588, "end_line": 1590, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Otot", "qualified_name": "Otot", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The total density parameter at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : Quantity-like ['redshift'], array-like, or `~numbers.Number`\n    Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOtot : ndarray or float\n    Returns float if input scalar. Value of 1.", "start_line": 1592, "end_line": 1607, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "_ScaleFactorMixin", "bases": [], "methods": ["scale_factor0", "scale_factor"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 69, "end_line": 98}, {"name": "FLRW", "bases": ["Cosmology", "_ScaleFactorMixin"], "methods": ["__init__", "Ob0", "m_nu", "is_flat", "Otot0", "Odm0", "Ok0", "Tnu0", "has_massive_nu", "h", "hubble_time", "hubble_distance", "critical_density0", "Ogamma0", "Onu0", "w", "Otot", "Om", "Ob", "Odm", "Ok", "Ode", "Ogamma", "Onu", "Tcmb", "Tnu", "nu_relative_density", "_w_integrand", "de_density_scale", "efunc", "inv_efunc", "_lookback_time_integrand_scalar", "lookback_time_integrand", "_abs_distance_integrand_scalar", "abs_distance_integrand", "H", "lookback_time", "_lookback_time", "_integral_lookback_time", "lookback_distance", "age", "_age", "_integral_age", "critical_density", "comoving_distance", "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2_scalar", "_integral_comoving_distance_z1z2", "comoving_transverse_dis