function uses the information in ``wcs.world_axis_object_classes`` and\n``wcs.world_axis_object_components`` to convert the high level objects\n(such as `~.SkyCoord`) to low level \"values\" `~.Quantity` objects.\n\nThis is used in `.HighLevel", "start_line": 121, "end_line": 243, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "values_to_high_level_objects", "qualified_name": "values_to_high_level_objects", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert low level values into high level objects.\n\nThis function uses the information in ``wcs.world_axis_object_classes`` and\n``wcs.world_axis_object_components`` to convert low level \"values\"\n`~.Quantity` objects, to high level objects (such as `~.SkyCoord).\n\nThis is used in `.HighLevelWCSMixin.pi", "start_line": 246, "end_line": 301, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "low_level_wcs", "qualified_name": "low_level_wcs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Returns a reference to the underlying low-level WCS object.", "start_line": 57, "end_line": 60, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_to_world", "qualified_name": "pixel_to_world", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Convert pixel coordinates to world coordinates (represented by\nhigh-level objects).\n\nIf a single high-level object is used to represent the world coordinates\n(i.e., if ``len(wcs.world_axis_object_classes) == 1``), it is returned\nas-is (not in a tuple/list), otherwise a tuple of high-level objects is", "start_line": 63, "end_line": 74, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "array_index_to_world", "qualified_name": "array_index_to_world", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert array indices to world coordinates (represented by Astropy\nobjects).\n\nIf a single high-level object is used to represent the world coordinates\n(i.e., if ``len(wcs.world_axis_object_classes) == 1``), it is returned\nas-is (not in a tuple/list), otherwise a tuple of high-level objects is\nreturn", "start_line": 76, "end_line": 88, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_to_pixel", "qualified_name": "world_to_pixel", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Convert world coordinates (represented by Astropy objects) to pixel\ncoordinates.\n\nIf `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` is ``1``, this\nmethod returns a single scalar or array, otherwise a tuple of scalars or\narrays is returned. See\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_to_pixel_v", "start_line": 91, "end_line": 101, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_to_array_index", "qualified_name": "world_to_array_index", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert world coordinates (represented by Astropy objects) to array\nindices.\n\nIf `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` is ``1``, this\nmethod returns a single scalar or array, otherwise a tuple of scalars or\narrays is returned. See\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_to_array_index", "start_line": 103, "end_line": 118, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "low_level_wcs", "qualified_name": "low_level_wcs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 312, "end_line": 313, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_to_pixel", "qualified_name": "world_to_pixel", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 315, "end_line": 323, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_to_world", "qualified_name": "pixel_to_world", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 325, "end_line": 339, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "BaseHighLevelWCS", "bases": [], "methods": ["low_level_wcs", "pixel_to_world", "array_index_to_world", "world_to_pixel", "world_to_array_index"], "docstring": "Abstract base class for the high-level WCS interface.\n\nThi