name": "world_n_dim", "qualified_name": "world_n_dim", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "The number of axes in the world coordinate system.", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 29, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_axis_physical_types", "qualified_name": "world_axis_physical_types", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "An iterable of strings describing the physical type for each world axis.\n\nThese should be names from the VO UCD1+ controlled Vocabulary\n(http://www.ivoa.net/documents/latest/UCDlist.html). If no matching UCD\ntype exists, this can instead be ``\"custom:xxx\"``, where ``xxx`` is an\narbitrary string.  Al", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 42, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_axis_units", "qualified_name": "world_axis_units", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "An iterable of strings given the units of the world coordinates for each\naxis.\n\nThe strings should follow the `IVOA VOUnit standard\n<http://ivoa.net/documents/VOUnits/>`_ (though as noted in the VOUnit\nspecification document, units that do not follow this standard are still\nallowed, but just not rec", "start_line": 46, "end_line": 55, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_to_world_values", "qualified_name": "pixel_to_world_values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Convert pixel coordinates to world coordinates.\n\nThis method takes `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` scalars or arrays as\ninput, and pixel coordinates should be zero-based. Returns\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_n_dim` scalars or arrays in units given by\n`~astropy.wcs.wcs", "start_line": 58, "end_line": 75, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "array_index_to_world_values", "qualified_name": "array_index_to_world_values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert array indices to world coordinates.\n\nThis is the same as `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_to_world_values` except that\nthe indices should be given in ``(i, j)`` order, where for an image\n``i`` is the row and ``j`` is the column (i.e. the opposite order to\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseL", "start_line": 77, "end_line": 90, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_to_pixel_values", "qualified_name": "world_to_pixel_values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Convert world coordinates to pixel coordinates.\n\nThis method takes `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_n_dim` scalars or arrays as\ninput in units given by `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_axis_units`. Returns\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` scalars or arrays. Note ", "start_line": 93, "end_line": 109, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_to_array_index_values", "qualified_name": "world_to_array_index_values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert world coordinates to array indices.\n\nThis is the same as `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_to_pixel_values` except that\nthe indices should be returned in ``(i, j)`` order, where for an image\n``i`` is the row and ``j`` is the column (i.e. the opposite order to\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.Ba", "start_line": 111, "end_line": 133, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_axis_object_components", "qualified_name": "world_axis_object_components", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "A list with `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_n_dim` elements giving information\non constructing high-level objects for the world coordinates.\n\nEach element of the list is a tuple with three items:\n\n* The first is a name for the world object this world array\n  corresponds to, which *must* m", "start_line": 137, "end_line": 166, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_axis_object_classes", "qualified_name": "world_axis_object_classes", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "A dictionary giving information on constructing high-level objects for\nthe world coordinates.\n\nEach key of the dictionary is a string key from\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_axis_object_components`, and each value is a\ntuple with three elements or four elements:\n\n* The first element of t", "start_line": 170, "end_line": 222, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "array_shape", "qualified_name": "array_shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The shape of the data that the WCS applies to as a tuple of length\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` in ``(row, column)``\norder (the convention for arrays in Python).\n\nIf the WCS is valid in the context of a dataset with a particular\nshape, then this property can be used to store the", "start_line": 228, "end_line": 243, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_shape", "qualified_name": "pixel_shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The shape of the data that the WCS applies to as a tuple of length\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim` in ``(x, y)``\norder (where for an image, ``x`` is the horizontal coordinate and ``y``\nis the vertical coordinate).\n\nIf the WCS is valid in the context of a dataset with a particular\ns", "start_line": 246, "end_line": 263, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_bounds", "qualified_name": "pixel_bounds", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The bounds (in pixel coordinates) inside which the WCS is defined,\nas a list with `~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim`\n``(min, max)`` tuples.\n\nThe bounds should be given in ``[(xmin, xmax), (ymin, ymax)]``\norder. WCS solutions are sometimes only guaranteed to be accurate\nwithin a certai", "start_line": 266, "end_line": 278, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_axis_names", "qualified_name": "pixel_axis_names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "An iterable of strings describing the name for each pixel axis.\n\nIf an axis does not have a name, an empty string should be returned\n(this is the default behavior for all axes if a subclass does not\noverride this property). Note that these names are just for display\npurposes and are not standardized", "start_line": 281, "end_line": 290, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "world_axis_names", "qualified_name": "world_axis_names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "An iterable of strings describing the name for each world axis.\n\nIf an axis does not have a name, an empty string should be returned\n(this is the default behavior for all axes if a subclass does not\noverride this property). Note that these names are just for display\npurposes and are not standardized", "start_line": 293, "end_line": 303, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "axis_correlation_matrix", "qualified_name": "axis_correlation_matrix", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns an (`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.world_n_dim`,\n`~astropy.wcs.wcsapi.BaseLowLevelWCS.pixel_n_dim`) matrix that\nindicates using booleans whether a given world coordinate depends on a\ngiven pixel coordinate.\n\nThis defaults to a matrix where all elements are `True` in the absence\nof any ", "start_line": 306, "end_line": 317, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "serialized_classes", "qualified_name": "serialized_classes", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Indicates whether Python objects are given in serialized form or as\nactual Python objects.", "start_line": 320, "end_line": 325, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_as_mpl_axes", "qualified_name": "_as_mpl_axes", "args": ["self"], "decora