ch larger than the oscillation period.\nIf you are searching for periods longer than the baseline of your\nobservatio", "start_line": 239, "end_line": 309, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "autopower", "qualified_name": "autopower", "args": ["self", "method", "sb_method", "normalization", "samples_per_peak", "nyquist_factor", "minimum_frequency", "maximum_frequency"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute Lomb-Scargle power at automatically-determined frequencies.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmethod : str, optional\n    specify the multi-band lomb scargle implementation to use. Options are:\n\n    - 'flexible': Constructs a common model, and an offset model per individual\n        band. Applies regular", "start_line": 311, "end_line": 385, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "power", "qualified_name": "power", "args": ["self", "frequency", "method", "sb_method", "normalization"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the Lomb-Scargle power at the given frequencies.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfrequency : array-like or `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['frequency']\n    frequencies (not angular frequencies) at which to evaluate the\n    periodogram. Note that in order to use method='fast', frequencies\n    must be regul", "start_line": 387, "end_line": 440, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "design_matrix", "qualified_name": "design_matrix", "args": ["self", "frequency", "t_fit", "bands_fit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the design matrix for a given frequency\n\nParameters\n----------\nfrequency : float\n    the frequency for the model\nt_fit : array-like, `~astropy.units.Quantity`, or `~astropy.time.Time` (optional)\n    Times (length ``n_samples``) at which to compute the model.\n    If not specified, then the ti", "start_line": 442, "end_line": 498, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "model", "qualified_name": "model", "args": ["self", "t", "frequency", "bands_fit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the Lomb-Scargle model at the given frequency.\n\nThe model at a particular frequency is a linear model:\nmodel = offset + dot(design_matrix, model_parameters)\n\nParameters\n----------\nt : array-like or `~astropy.units.Quantity` ['time']\n    Times (length ``n_samples``) at which to compute the mo", "start_line": 500, "end_line": 546, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "offset", "qualified_name": "offset", "args": ["self", "t_fit", "bands_fit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the offset array of the model\n\nThe offset array of the model is the (weighted) mean of the y values in each band.\nNote that if self.center_data is False, the offset is 0 by definition.\n\nParameters\n----------\nt_fit : array-like, `~astropy.units.Quantity`, or `~astropy.time.Time` (optional)\n   ", "start_line": 548, "end_line": 619, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "model_parameters", "qualified_name": "model_parameters", "args": ["self", "frequency", "units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the best-fit model parameters at the given frequency.\n\nThe model described by these parameters is:\n\n.. math::\n\n    y(t; f, \\vec{\\theta}) = \\theta_0 + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\tt nterms_base} [\\theta_{2n-1}\\sin(2\\pi n f t) + \\theta_{2n}\\cos(2\\pi n f t)]\n    + \\theta_0^{(k)} + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\tt nterms_band}", "start_line": 621, "end_line": 693, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "false_alarm_probability", "qualified_name": "false_alarm_probability", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Not Implemented", "start_line": 695, "end_line": 697, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "false_alarm_level", "qualified_name": "false_alarm_level", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Not Implemented", "start_line": 699, "end_line": 701, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "distribution", "qualified_name": "distribution", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Not Implemented", "sta