 and the unit of the ufunc result.\n\nConverters are functions required to convert to a ufunc's expected unit,\ne.g., radian for np.sin; or to ensure units of two inputs are consistent,\ne.g., for np.add.  In these examples, the unit of the result would be\ndimensionless_", "start_line": 141, "end_line": 289, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_output", "qualified_name": "check_output", "args": ["output", "unit", "inputs", "function"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check that function output can be stored in the output array given.\n\nParameters\n----------\noutput : array or `~astropy.units.Quantity` or tuple\n    Array that should hold the function output (or tuple of such arrays).\nunit : `~astropy.units.Unit` or None, or tuple\n    Unit that the output will have,", "start_line": 292, "end_line": 392, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 37, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "register_module", "qualified_name": "register_module", "args": ["self", "module", "names", "importer"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Register (but do not import) a set of ufunc helpers.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodule : str\n    Name of the module with the ufuncs (e.g., 'scipy.special').\nnames : iterable of str\n    Names of the module ufuncs for which helpers are available.\nimporter : callable\n    Function that imports the ufuncs an", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 54, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "import_module", "qualified_name": "import_module", "args": ["self", "module"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Import the helpers from the given module using its helper function.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodule : str\n    Name of the module. Has to have been registered beforehand.", "start_line": 56, "end_line": 66, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__missing__", "qualified_name": "__missing__", "args": ["self", "ufunc"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Called if a ufunc is not found.\n\nCheck if the ufunc is in any of the available modules, and, if so,\nimport the helpers for that module.", "start_line": 68, "end_line": 103, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setitem__", "qualified_name": "__setitem__", "args": ["self", "key", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 105, "end_line": 116, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "UfuncHelpers", "bases": ["dict"], "methods": ["__init__", "register_module", "import_module", "__missing__", "__setitem__"], "docstring": "Registry of unit conversion functions to help ufunc evaluation.\n\nBased on dict for quick access, but with a missing method to load\nhelpers for additional modules such as scipy.special and erfa.\n\nSuch modules should be registered using ``register_module``.", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 116}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Converters for Quantity.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/quantity_helper/erfa.py", "file_hash": "10d62bb96deec05f8b46a1bcc0f524e04a62f6f233d0732a8aa36c016581558f", "imports": [{"module": "erfa", "names": ["dt_eraASTROM", "dt_eraLDBODY", "dt_pv"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "erfa", "names": ["ufunc"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.units.core", "names": ["UnitsError", "UnitTypeError", "dimensionless_unscaled"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.units.structured", "names": ["StructuredUnit"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["UFUNC_HELPERS"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "helpers", "names": ["_d", "get_converter", "helper_invariant", "helper_multiplication", "helper_twoarg_invariant"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.units.si", "names": ["radian"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.units.si", "names": ["radian"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "ast