", "args": ["arr", "dtype"], "decorators": ["function_helper(module=np.lib.recfunctions)"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1185, "end_line": 1190, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_izip_units_flat", "qualified_name": "_izip_units_flat", "args": ["iterable"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns an iterator of collapsing any nested unit structure.\n\nParameters\n----------\niterable : Iterable[StructuredUnit | Unit] or StructuredUnit\n    A structured unit or iterable thereof.\n\nYields\n------\nunit", "start_line": 1193, "end_line": 1215, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "merge_arrays", "qualified_name": "merge_arrays", "args": ["seqarrays", "fill_value", "flatten", "usemask", "asrecarray"], "decorators": ["function_helper(helps=rfn.merge_arrays)"], "docstring": "Merge structured Quantities field by field.\n\nLike :func:`numpy.lib.recfunctions.merge_arrays`. Note that ``usemask`` and\n``asrecarray`` are not supported at this time and will raise a ValueError if\nnot `False`.", "start_line": 1219, "end_line": 1267, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "assignments"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 141, "end_line": 142, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self", "f", "helps", "module"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add a helper to a numpy function.\n\nNormally used as a decorator.\n\nIf ``helps`` is given, it should be the numpy function helped (or an\niterable of numpy functions helped).\n\nIf ``helps`` is not given, it is assumed the function helped is the\nnumpy function with the same name as the decorated function", "start_line": 144, "end_line": 166, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "median", "qualified_name": "median", "args": ["a", "axis", "out", "overwrite_input", "keepdims"], "decorators": ["function_helper"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 386, "end_line": 397, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "replace_unit", "qualified_name": "replace_unit", "args": ["x"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1156, "end_line": 1160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "FunctionAssigner", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 140, "end_line": 166}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Helpers for overriding numpy functions.\n\nWe override numpy functions in `~astropy.units.Quantity.__array_function__`.\nIn this module, the numpy functions are split in four groups, each of\nwhich has an associated `set` or `dict`:\n\n1. SUBCLASS_SAFE_FUNCTIONS (set), if the numpy implementation\n   supports Quantity; we pass on to ndarray.__array_function__.\n2. FUNCTION_HELPERS (dict), if the numpy implementation is usable\n   after converting quantities to arrays with suitable units,\n   and possibly setting units on the result.\n3. DISPATCHED_FUNCTIONS (dict), if the function makes sense but\n   requires a Quantity-specific implementation\n4. UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTIONS (set), if the function does not make sense.\n\nFor the FUNCTION_HELPERS `dict`, the value is a function that does the\nunit conversion.  It should take the same arguments as the numpy\nfunction would (though one can use ``*args`` and ``**kwargs``) and\nreturn a tuple of ``args, kwargs, unit, out``, where ``args`` and\n``kwargs`` will be will be passed on to the numpy implementation,\n``unit`` is a possible unit of the result (`None` if it should not be\nconverted to Quantity), and ``out`` is a possible output Quantity passed\nin, which will be filled in-place.\n\nFor the DISPATCHED_FUNCTIONS `dict`, the value is a function that\nimplements the numpy functionality for Quantity input. It should\nreturn a tuple of ``result, unit, out``, where ``result`` is generally\na plain array with the result, and ``unit`` and ``out`` are as above.\nIf unit is `None`, result gets returned directly, so one can also\nreturn a Quantity directly using ``quantity_result, None, None``.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/function/__init__.py", "file_hash": "eea37a0a2cd3dea0a039c068a05e342cf8683b3238d5652c1691680be15a2377", "imports": [{"module": "core", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "logarithmic", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This subpackage contains classes and functions for defining and converting\nbetween different function units and quantities, i.e., using units which\nare some function of a physical unit, such as magnitudes and decibels.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/function/mixin.py", "file_hash": "016cf3223b37ccda1f2f115381024a7a86963885006c8abf4ec69ff47b0458bb", "imports": [{"module": "astropy.units.core", "names": ["IrreducibleUnit", "Unit"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 16, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "FunctionMixin", "bases": [], "methods": ["__call__"], "docstring": "Mixin class that makes UnitBase subclasses callable.\n\nProvides a __call__ method that passes on arguments to a FunctionUnit.\nInstances of this class should define ``_function_unit_class`` pointing\nto the relevant class.\n\nSee units.py and logarithmic.py for usage.", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 16}, {"name": "IrreducibleFunctionUnit", "bases": ["FunctionMixin", "IrreducibleUnit"], "methods": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 20}, {"name": "RegularFunctionUnit", "bases": ["FunctionMixin", "Unit"], "methods": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 24}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/function/logarithmic.py", "file_hash": "de44d6c18144d601d6c930b34a07647a4ebe2d55f41bc67da5c02f74e330fa71", "imports": [{"module": "numbers", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy.units", "names": ["CompositeUnit", "Unit", "UnitConversionError", "UnitsError", "UnitTypeError", "dimensionless_unscaled", "photometric"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["FunctionQuantity", "FunctionUnitBase"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "units", "names": ["dB", "dex", "mag"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "_default_function_unit", "qualified_name": "_default_function_unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 55, "end_line": 56, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_quantity_class", "qualified_name": "_quantity_class", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 59, "end_line": 60, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "from_physical", "qualified_name": "from_physical", "args": ["self", "x"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Transformation from value in physical to value in logarithmic units.\nUsed in equivalency.", "start_line": 62, "end_line": 66, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_physical", "qualified_name": "to_physical", "args": ["self", "x"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Transformation from value in logarithmic to value in physical units.\nUsed in equivalency.", "start_line": 68, "end_line": 72, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_add_and_adjust_physical_unit", "qualified_name": "_add_and_adjust_physical_unit", "args": ["self", "other", "sign_self", "sign_other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add/subtract LogUnit to/from another unit, and adjust physical unit.\n\nself and other are multiplied by sign_self and sign_other, resp.\n\nWe wish to do:   \u00b1lu_1 + \u00b1lu_2  -> lu_f          (lu=logarithmic unit)\n          and     pu_1^(\u00b11) * pu_2^(\u00b11) -> pu_f  (pu=physical uni