", "start_line": 301, "end_line": 351, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_fetch", "qualified_name": "_fetch", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper function to fetch values from owning section.\n\nReturns a 2-tuple: the value, and the section where it was found.", "start_line": 354, "end_line": 385, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse_match", "qualified_name": "_parse_match", "args": ["self", "match"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Implementation-dependent helper function.\n\nWill be passed a match object corresponding to the interpolation\nkey we just found (e.g., \"%(foo)s\" or \"$foo\"). Should look up that\nkey in the appropriate config file section (using the ``_fetch()``\nhelper function) and return a 3-tuple: (key, value, sectio", "start_line": 388, "end_line": 404, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse_match", "qualified_name": "_parse_match", "args": ["self", "match"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 413, "end_line": 416, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse_match", "qualified_name": "_parse_match", "args": ["self", "match"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 432, "end_line": 443, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setstate__", "qualified_name": "__setstate__", "args": ["self", "state"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 475, "end_line": 477, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 479, "end_line": 481, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "parent", "depth", "main", "indict", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "* parent is the section above\n* depth is the depth level of this section\n* main is the main ConfigObj\n* indict is a dictionary to initialise the section with", "start_line": 484, "end_line": 507, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_initialise", "qualified_name": "_initialise", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 510, "end_line": 524, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_interpolate", "qualified_name": "_interpolate", "args": ["self", "key", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 527, "end_line": 547, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Fetch the item and do string interpolation.", "start_line": 550, "end_line": 564, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setitem__", "qualified_name": "__setitem__", "args": ["self", "key", "value", "unrepr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Correctly set a value.\n\nMaking dictionary values Section instances.\n(We have to special case 'Section' instances - which are also dicts)\n\nKeys must be strings.\nValues need only be strings (or lists of strings) if\n``main.stringify`` is set.\n\n``unrepr`` must be set when setting a value to a dictionary", "start_line": 567, "end_line": 623, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__delitem__", "qualified_name": "__delitem__", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove items from the sequence when deleting.", "start_line": 626, "end_line": 634, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get", "qualified_name": "get", "args": ["self", "key", "default"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A version of ``get`` that doesn't bypass string interpolation.", "start_line": 637, "end_line": 642, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update", "qualified_name": "update", "args": ["self", "indict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A version of update that uses our ``__setitem__``.", "start_line": 645, "end_line": 650, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pop", "qualified_name": "pop", "args": ["self", "key", "default"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "'D.pop(k[,d]) -> v, remove specified key and return the corresponding value.\nIf key is not found, d is returned if given, otherwise KeyError is raised'", "start_line": 653, "end_line": 666, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "popitem", "qualified_name": "popitem", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Pops the first (key,val)", "start_line": 669, "end_line": 677, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear", "qualified_name": "clear", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A version of clear that also affects scalars/sections\nAlso clears comments and configspec.\n\nLeaves other attributes alone :\n    depth/main/parent are not affected", "start_line": 680, "end_line": 695, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "setdefault", "qualified_name": "setdefault", "args": ["self", "key", "default"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A version of setdefault that sets sequence if appropriate.", "start_line": 698, "end_line": 704, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "items", "qualified_name": "items", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.items() -> list of D's (key, value) pairs, as 2-tuples", "start_line": 707, "end_line": 709, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "keys", "qualified_name": "keys", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.keys() -> list of D's keys", "start_line": 712, "end_line": 714, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "values", "qualified_name": "values", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.values() -> list of D's values", "start_line": 717, "end_line": 719, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "iteritems", "qualified_name": "iteritems", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.iteritems() -> an iterator over the (key, value) items of D", "start_line": 722, "end_line": 724, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "iterkeys", "qualified_name": "iterkeys", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.iterkeys() -> an iterator over the keys of D", "start_line": 727, "end_line": 729, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "itervalues", "qualified_name": "itervalues", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "D.itervalues() -> an iterator over the values of D", "start_line": 734, "end_line": 736, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "x.__repr__() <==> repr(x)", "start_line": 739, "end_line": 747, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dict", "qualified_name": "dict", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a deepcopy of self as a dictionary.\n\nAll members that are ``Section`` instances are recursively turned to\nordinary dictionaries - by calling their ``dict`` method.\n\n>>> n = a.dict()\n>>> n == a\n1\n>>> n is a\n0", "start_line": 755, "end_line": 780, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "merge", "qualified_name": "merge", "args": ["self", "indict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A recursive update - useful for merging config files.\n\n>>> a = '''[section1]\n...     option1 = True\n...     [[subsection]]\n...     more_options = False\n...     # end of file'''.splitlines()\n>>> b = '''# File is user.ini\n...     [section1]\n...     option1 = False\n...     # end of file'''.splitlines()", "start_line": 783, "end_line": 807, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "rename", "qualified_name": "rename", "args": ["self", "oldkey", "newkey"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Change a keyname to another, without changing position in sequence.\n\nImplemented so that transformations can be made on keys,\nas well as on values. (used by encode and decode)\n\nAlso renames comments.", "start_line": 810, "end_line": 837, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "walk", "qualified_name": "walk", "args": ["self", "function", "raise_errors", "call_on_sections"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Walk every member and call a function on the keyword and value.\n\nReturn a dictionary of the return values\n\nIf the function raises an exception, raise the errror\nunless ``raise_errors=False``, in which case set the return value to\n``False``.\n\nAny unrecognized keyword arguments you pass to walk, will ", "start_line": 840, "end_line": 922, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_bool", "qualified_name": "as_bool", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Accepts a key as input. The corresponding value must be a string or\nthe objects (``True`` or 1) or (``False`` or 0). We allow 0 and 1 to\nretain compatibility with Python 2.2.\n\nIf the string is one of  ``True``, ``On``, ``Yes``, or ``1`` it returns\n``True``.\n\nIf the string is one of  ``False``, ``Off", "start_line": 925, "end_line": 966, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_int", "qualified_name": "as_int", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A convenience method which coerces the specified value to an integer.\n\nIf the value is an invalid literal for ``int``, a ``ValueError`` will\nbe raised.\n\n>>> a = ConfigObj()\n>>> a['a'] = 'fish'\n>>> a.as_int('a')\nTraceback (most recent call last):\nValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'f", "start_line": 969, "end_line": 989, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_float", "qualified_name": "as_float", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A convenience method which coerces the specified value to a float.\n\nIf the value is an invalid literal for ``float``, a ``ValueError`` will\nbe raised.\n\n>>> a = ConfigObj()\n>>> a['a'] = 'fish'\n>>> a.as_float('a')  #doctest: +IGNORE_EXCEPTION_DETAIL\nTraceback (most recent call last):\nValueError: inval", "start_line": 992, "end_line": 1011, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_list", "qualified_name": "as_list", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A convenience method which fetches the specified value, guaranteeing\nthat it is a list.\n\n>>> a = ConfigObj()\n>>> a['a'] = 1\n>>> a.as_list('a')\n[1]\n>>> a['a'] = (1,)\n>>> a.as_list('a')\n[1]\n>>> a['a'] = [1]\n>>> a.as_list('a')\n[1]", "start_line": 1014, "end_line": 1033, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "restore_default", "qualified_name": "restore_default", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Restore (and return) default value for the specified key.\n\nThis method will only work for a ConfigObj that was created\nwith a configspec and has been validated.\n\nIf there is no default value for this key, ``KeyError`` is raised.", "start_line": 1036, "end_line": 1049, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "restore_defaults", "qualified_name": "restore_defaults", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Recursively restore default values to all members\nthat have them.\n\nThis method will only work for a ConfigObj that was created\nwith a configspec and has been validated.\n\nIt doesn't delete or modify entries without default values.", "start_line": 1052, "end_line": 1066, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "infile", "options", "configspec", "encoding", "interpolation", "raise_errors", "list_values", "create_empty", "file_error", "stringify", "indent_type", "default_encoding", "unrepr", "write_empty_values", "_inspec"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parse a config file or create a config file object.\n\n``ConfigObj(infile=None, configspec=None, encoding=None,\n            interpolation=True, raise_errors=False, list_values=True,\n            create_empty=False, file_error=False, stringify=True,\n            indent_type=None, default_encoding=None, u", "start_line": 1172, "end_line": 1227, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_load", "qualified_name": "_load", "args": ["self", "infile", "configspec"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1230, "end_line": 1323, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_initialise", "qualified_name": "_initialise", "args": ["self", "options"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1326, "end_line": 1355, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1358, "end_line": 1366, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_bom", "qualified_name": "_handle_bom", "args": ["self", "infile"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Handle any BOM, and decode if necessary.\n\nIf an encoding is specified, that *must* be used - but the BOM should\nstill be removed (and the BOM attribute set).\n\n(If the encoding is wrongly specified, then a BOM for an alternative\nencoding won't be discovered or removed.)\n\nIf an encoding is not specifi", "start_line": 1369, "end_line": 1478, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_a_to_u", "qualified_name": "_a_to_u", "args": ["self", "aString"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Decode ASCII strings to unicode if a self.encoding is specified.", "start_line": 1481, "end_line": 1486, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_decode", "qualified_name": "_decode", "args": ["self", "infile", "encoding"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Decode infile to unicode. Using the specified encoding.\n\nif is a string, it also needs converting to a list.", "start_line": 1489, "end_line": 1511, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_decode_element", "qualified_name": "_decode_element", "args": ["self", "line"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Decode element to unicode if necessary.", "start_line": 1514, "end_line": 1519, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_str", "qualified_name": "_str", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Used by ``stringify`` within validate, to turn non-string values\ninto strings.", "start_line": 1523, "end_line": 1533, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse", "qualified_name": "_parse", "args": ["self", "infile"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Actually parse the config file.", "start_line": 1536, "end_line": 1700, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_match_depth", "qualified_name": "_match_depth", "args": ["self", "sect", "depth"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a section and a depth level, walk back through the sections\nparents to see if the depth level matches a previous section.\n\nReturn a reference to the right section,\nor raise a SyntaxError.", "start_line": 1703, "end_line": 1719, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_error", "qualified_name": "_handle_error", "args": ["self", "text", "ErrorClass", "infile", "cur_index"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Handle an error according to the error settings.\n\nEither raise the error or store it.\nThe error will have occured at ``cur_index``", "start_line": 1722, "end_line": 1738, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_unquote", "qualified_name": "_unquote", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an unquoted version of a value", "start_line": 1741, "end_line": 1748, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_quote", "qualified_name": "_quote", "args": ["self", "value", "multiline"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a safely quoted version of a value.\n\nRaise a ConfigObjError if the value cannot be safely quoted.\nIf multiline is ``True`` (default) then use triple quotes\nif necessary.\n\n* Don't quote values that don't need it.\n* Recursively quote members of a list and return a comma joined list.\n* Multiline", "start_line": 1751, "end_line": 1819, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_single_quote", "qualified_name": "_get_single_quote", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1822, "end_line": 1829, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_triple_quote", "qualified_name": "_get_triple_quote", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1832, "end_line": 1839, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_value", "qualified_name": "_handle_value", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a value string, unquote, remove comment,\nhandle lists. (including empty and single member lists)", "start_line": 1842, "end_line": 1888, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_multiline", "qualified_name": "_multiline", "args": ["self", "value", "infile", "cur_index", "maxline"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Extract the value, where we are in a multiline situation.", "start_line": 1891, "end_line": 1923, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_configspec", "qualified_name": "_handle_configspec", "args": ["self", "configspec"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parse the configspec.", "start_line": 1926, "end_line": 1943, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_configspec", "qualified_name": "_set_configspec", "args": ["self", "section", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Called by validate. Handles setting the configspec on subsections\nincluding sections to be validated by __many__", "start_line": 1947, "end_line": 1972, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_write_line", "qualified_name": "_write_line", "args": ["self", "indent_string", "entry", "this_entry", "comment"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Write an individual line, for the write method", "start_line": 1975, "end_line": 1986, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_write_marker", "qualified_name": "_write_marker", "args": ["self", "indent_string", "depth", "entry", "comment"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Write a section marker line", "start_line": 1989, "end_line": 1995, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_comment", "qualified_name": "_handle_comment", "args": ["self", "comment"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Deal with a comment.", "start_line": 1998, "end_line": 2005, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name": "write", "args": ["self", "outfile", "section"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Write the current ConfigObj as a file\n\ntekNico: FIXME: use StringIO instead of real files\n\n>>> filename = a.filename\n>>> a.filename = 'test.ini'\n>>> a.write()\n>>> a.filename = filename\n>>> a == ConfigObj('test.ini', raise_errors=True)\n1\n>>> import os\n>>> os.remove('test.ini')", "start_line": 2010, "end_line": 2122, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate", "qualified_name": "validate", "args": ["self", "validator", "preserve_errors", "copy", "section"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test the ConfigObj against a configspec.\n\nIt uses the ``validator`` object from *validate.py*.\n\nTo run ``validate`` on the current ConfigObj, call: ::\n\n    test = config.validate(validator)\n\n(Normally having previously passed in the configspec when the ConfigObj\nwas created - you can dynamically ass", "start_line": 2124, "end_line": 2328, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reset", "qualified_name": "reset", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear ConfigObj instance and restore to 'freshly created' state.", "start_line": 2331, "end_line": 2339, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload", "qualified_name": "reload", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reload a ConfigObj from file.\n\nThis method raises a ``ReloadError`` if the ConfigObj doesn't have\na filename attribute pointing to a file.", "start_line": 2342, "end_line": 2364, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2380, "end_line": 2381, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check", "qualified_name": "check", "args": ["self", "check", "member", "missing"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A dummy check method, always returns the value unchanged.", "start_line": 2383, "end_line": 2387, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "recursive_interpolate", "qualified_name": "recursive_interpolate", "args": ["key", "value", "section", "backtrail"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The function that does the actual work.\n\n``value``: the string we're trying to interpolate.\n``section``: the section in which that string was found\n``backtrail``: a dict to keep track of where we've been,\nto detect and prevent infinite recursion loops\n\nThis is similar to a depth-first-search algorit", "start_line": 306, "end_line": 346, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_getval", "qualified_name": "_getval", "args": ["key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 741, "end_line": 745, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_getval", "qualified_name": "_getval", "args": ["key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1359, "end_line": 1363, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate_entry", "qualified_name": "validate_entry", "args": ["entry", "spec", "val", "missing", "ret_true", "ret_false"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2185, "end_line": 2227, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_check", "qualified_name": "_check", "args": ["entry"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 557, "end_line": 560, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_section", "qualified_name": "set_section", "args": ["in_section", "this_section"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1256, "end_line": 1261, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "UnknownType", "bases": ["Exception"], "methods": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 135, "end_line": 136}, {"name": "Builder", "bases": ["object"], "methods": ["build", "build_List", "build_Const", "build_Dict", "build_Tuple", "build_Name", "build_Add", "build_Getattr", "build_UnarySub", "build_UnaryAdd"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 139, "end_line": 191}, {"name": "ConfigObjError", "bases": ["SyntaxError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "This is the base class for all errors that ConfigObj raises.\nIt is a subclass of SyntaxError.", "start_line": 206, "end_line": 214}, {"name": "NestingError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "This error indicates a level of nesting that doesn't match.", "start_line": 217, "end_line": 220}, {"name": "ParseError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "This error indicates that a line is badly written.\nIt is neither a valid ``key = value`` line,\nnor a valid section marker line.", "start_line": 223, "end_line": 228}, {"name": "ReloadError", "bases": ["IOError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "A 'reload' operation failed.\nThis exception is a subclass of ``IOError``.", "start_line": 231, "end_line": 237}, {"name": "DuplicateError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "The keyword or section specified already exists.", "start_line": 240, "end_line": 243}, {"name": "ConfigspecError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "An error occured whilst parsing a configspec.", "start_line": 246, "end_line": 249}, {"name": "InterpolationError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Base class for the two interpolation errors.", "start_line": 252, "end_line": 253}, {"name": "InterpolationLoopError", "bases": ["InterpolationError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Maximum interpolation depth exceeded in string interpolation.", "start_line": 256, "end_line": 262}, {"name": "RepeatSectionError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "This error indicates additional sections in a section with a\n``__many__`` (repeated) section.", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 269}, {"name": "MissingInterpolationOption", "bases": ["InterpolationError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "A value specified for interpolation was missing.", "start_line": 272, "end_line": 276}, {"name": "UnreprError", "bases": ["ConfigObjError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "An error parsing in unrepr mode.", "start_line": 279, "end_line": 280}, {"name": "InterpolationEngine", "bases": ["object"], "methods": ["__init__", "interpolate", "_fetch", "_parse_match"], "docstring": "A helper class to help perform string interpolation.\n\nThis class is an abstract base class; its descendants perform\nthe actual work.", "start_line": 284, "end_line": 404}, {"name": "ConfigParserInterpolation", "bases": ["InterpolationEngine"], "methods": ["_parse_match"], "docstring": "Behaves like ConfigParser.", "start_line": 408, "end_line": 416}, {"name": "TemplateInterpolation", "bases": ["InterpolationEngine"], "methods": ["_parse_match"], "docstring": "Behaves like string.Template.", "start_line": 420, "end_line": 443}, {"name": "Section", "bases": ["dict"], "methods": ["__setstate__", "__reduce__", "__init__", "_initialise", "_interpolate", "__getitem__", "__setitem__", "__delitem__", "get", "update", "pop", "popitem", "clear", "setdefault", "items", "keys", "values", "iteritems", "iterkeys", "itervalues", "__repr__", "dict", "merge", "rename", "walk", "as_bool", "as_int", "as_float", "as_list", "restore_default", "restore_defaults"], "docstring": "A dictionary-like object that represents a section in a config file.\n\nIt does string interpolation if the 'interpolation' attribute\nof the 'main' object is set to True.\n\nInterpolation is tried first from this object, then from the 'DEFAULT'\nsection of this object, next from the parent and its 'DEFAU", "start_line": 456, "end_line": 1066}, {"name": "ConfigObj", "bases": ["Section"], "methods": ["__init__", "_load", "_initialise", "__repr__", "_handle_bom", "_a_to_u", "_decode", "_decode_element", "_str", "_parse", "_match_depth", "_handle_error", "_unquote", "_quote", "_get_single_quote", "_get_triple_quote", "_handle_value", "_mu