rue) equinox of J2000, and the xy-plane in the plane of the\necliptic of J2000 (according to the IAU 1976/1980 obliquity model).", "start_line": 226, "end_line": 242}, {"name": "CustomBarycentricEcliptic", "bases": ["BaseEclipticFrame"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Barycentric ecliptic coordinates with custom obliquity.\nThese origin of the coordinates are the\nbarycenter of the solar system, with the x axis pointing in the direction of\nthe *mean* (not true) equinox of J2000, and the xy-plane in the plane of the\necliptic tilted a custom obliquity angle.\n\nThe fra", "start_line": 246, "end_line": 257}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/coordinates/tests/test_api_ape5.py", "file_hash": "438ed2fb23b4dfeb4284133c0e8d0e2caeb63287f48924871fe5ed8304ca3cf4", "imports": [{"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "pytest", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": ["testing"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["coordinates"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["time"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.tests.helper", "names": ["assert_quantity_allclose"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.units", "names": ["allclose"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.compat.optional_deps", "names": ["HAS_SCIPY"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.coordinates", "names": ["Angle", "Distance", "Latitude", "Longitude"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.coordinates.representation", "names": ["CartesianRepresentation", "PhysicsSphericalRepresentation", "SphericalRepresentation", "UnitSphericalRepresentation"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.coordinates.builtin_frames", "names": ["FK5", "ICRS"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astro