t_teme_itrf", "qualified_name": "test_teme_itrf", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test case transform from TEME to ITRF.\n\nTest case derives from example on appendix C of Vallado, Crawford, Hujsak & Kelso (2006).\nSee https://celestrak.com/publications/AIAA/2006-6753/AIAA-2006-6753-Rev2.pdf", "start_line": 748, "end_line": 802, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_precessedgeocentric_loopback", "qualified_name": "test_precessedgeocentric_loopback", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 805, "end_line": 840, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_teme_loopback", "qualified_name": "test_teme_loopback", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 843, "end_line": 854, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_earth_orientation_table", "qualified_name": "test_earth_orientation_table", "args": ["monkeypatch"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.remote_data"], "docstring": "Check that we can set the IERS table used as Earth Reference.\n\nUse the here and now to be sure we get a difference.", "start_line": 858, "end_line": 891, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_ephemerides", "qualified_name": "test_ephemerides", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.remote_data", "pytest.mark.skipif(not HAS_JPLEPHEM, reason='requires jplephem')"], "docstring": "We test that using different ephemerides gives very similar results\nfor transformations", "start_line": 896, "end_line": 940, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_tete_transforms", "qualified_name": "test_tete_transforms", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "We test the TETE transforms for proper behaviour here.\n\nThe TETE transforms are tested for accuracy against JPL Horizons in\ntest_solar_system.py. Here we are looking to check for consistency and\nerrors in the self transform.", "start_line": 943, "end_line": 983, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_straight_overhead", "qualified_name": "test_straight_overhead", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "With a precise CIRS<->Observed transformation this should give Alt=90 exactly\n\nIf the CIRS self-transform breaks it won't, due to improper treatment of aberration", "start_line": 986, "end_line": 1018, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_itrs_straight_overhead", "qualified_name": "test_itrs_straight_overhead", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "With a precise ITRS<->Observed transformation this should give Alt=90 exactly", "start_line": 1021, "end_line": 1037, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "jplephem_ge", "qualified_name": "jplephem_ge", "args": ["minversion"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check if jplephem is installed and has version >= minversion.", "start_line": 1040, "end_line": 1048, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_aa_hd_high_precision", "qualified_name": "test_aa_hd_high_precision", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.remote_data", "pytest.mark.skipif(not jplephem_ge('2.15'), reason='requires jplephem >= 2.15')"], "docstring": "These tests are provided by @mkbrewer - see issue #10356.\n\nThe code that produces them agrees very well (<0.5 mas) with SkyField once Polar motion\nis turned off, but SkyField does not include polar motion, so a comparison to Skyfield\nor JPL Horizons will be ~1\" off.\n\nThe absence of polar motion with", "start_line": 1053, "end_line": 1104, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_aa_high_precision_nodata", "qualified_name": "test_aa_high_precision_nodata", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "These tests are designed to ensure high precision alt-az transforms.\n\nThey are a slight fudge since the target values come from astropy itself. They are generated\nwith a version of the code that passes the tests above, but for the internal solar system\nephemerides to avoid the use of remote data.", "start_line": 1107, "end_line": 1126, "is_async": fals