er_class", "differential_class"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert coordinates to another representation.\n\nIf the instance is of the requested class, it is returned unmodified.\nBy default, conversion is done via Cartesian coordinates.\nAlso note that orientation information at the origin is *not* preserved by\nconversions through Cartesian coordinates. See th", "start_line": 849, "end_line": 889, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "transform", "qualified_name": "transform", "args": ["self", "matrix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Transform coordinates using a 3x3 matrix in a Cartesian basis.\n\nThis returns a new representation and does not modify the original one.\nAny differentials attached to this representation will also be\ntransformed.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmatrix : (3,3) array-like\n    A 3x3 (or stack thereof) matrix, su", "start_line": 891, "end_line": 915, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "with_differentials", "qualified_name": "with_differentials", "args": ["self", "differentials"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new representation with the same positions as this\nrepresentation, but with these new differentials.\n\nDifferential keys that already exist in this object's differential dict\nare overwritten.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndifferentials : sequence of `~astropy.coordinates.BaseDifferential` subclass ", "start_line": 917, "end_line": 948, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "without_differentials", "qualified_name": "without_differentials", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a copy of the representation without attached differentials.\n\nReturns\n-------\n`~astropy.coordinates.BaseRepresentation` subclass instance\n    A shallow copy of this representation, without any differentials.\n    If no differentials were present, no copy is made.", "start_line": 950, "end_line": 963, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "from_representation", "qualified_