 "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_reader", "qualified_name": "get_reader", "args": ["Reader", "Inputter", "Outputter"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Initialize a table reader allowing for common customizations.  Most of the\ndefault behavior for various parameters is determined by the Reader class.\n\nParameters\n----------\nReader : `~astropy.io.ascii.BaseReader`\n    Reader class (DEPRECATED). Default is :class:`Basic`.\nInputter : `~astropy.io.ascii", "start_line": 121, "end_line": 184, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_format_class", "qualified_name": "_get_format_class", "args": ["format", "ReaderWriter", "label"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 187, "end_line": 200, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_fast_reader_dict", "qualified_name": "_get_fast_reader_dict", "args": ["kwargs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert 'fast_reader' key in kwargs into a dict if not already and make sure\n'enable' key is available.", "start_line": 203, "end_line": 212, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_validate_read_write_kwargs", "qualified_name": "_validate_read_write_kwargs", "args": ["read_write"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Validate types of keyword arg inputs to read() or write().", "start_line": 215, "end_line": 262, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_expand_user_if_path", "qualified_name": "_expand_user_if_path", "args": ["argument"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 279, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "read", "qualified_name": "read", "args": ["table", "guess"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 282, "end_line": 443, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_guess", "qualified_name": "_guess", "args": ["table", "read_kwargs", "format", "fast_reader"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Try to read the table using various sets of keyword args.  Start with the\nstandard guess list and filter to make it unique and consistent with\nuser-supplied read keyword args.  Finally, if none of those work then\ntry the original user-supplied keyword args.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntable : str, file-l", "start_line": 449, "end_line": 650, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_guess_kwargs_list", "qualified_name": "_get_guess_kwargs_list", "args": ["read_kwargs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the full list of reader keyword argument dicts.\n\nThese are the basis for the format guessing process.\nThe returned full list will then be:\n\n- Filtered to be consistent with user-supplied kwargs\n- Cleaned to have only unique entries\n- Used one by one to try reading the input table\n\nNote that the ", "start_line": 653, "end_line": 730, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_read_in_chunks", "qualified_name": "_read_in_chunks", "args": ["table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "For fast_reader read the ``table`` in chunks and vstack to create\na single table, OR return a generator of chunk tables.", "start_line": 733, "end_line": 779, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_read_in_chunks_generator", "qualified_name": "_read_in_chunks_generator", "args": ["table", "chunk_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "For fast_reader read the ``table`` in chunks and return a generator\nof tables for each chunk.", "start_line": 782, "end_line": 850, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_writer", "qualified_name": "get_writer", "args": ["Writer", "fast_writer"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Initialize a table writer allowing for common customizations.  Most of the\ndefault behavior for various parameters is determined by the Writer class.\n\nParameters\n----------\nWriter : ``Writer``\n    Writer class (DEPRECATED). Defaults to :class:`Basic`.\ndelimiter : str\n    Column delimiter string\ncomm", "start_line": 865, "end_line": 919, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name":