n, initialize a new `FITS_rec`\nobject.\n\n.. note::\n\n    This was originally part of the ``new_table`` function in the table\n    module but was moved into a class method since most of its\n    functionality always had more to do with initializing a `FITS_rec`\n  ", "start_line": 282, "end_line": 481, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 483, "end_line": 486, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getattribute__", "qualified_name": "__getattribute__", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 488, "end_line": 506, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 508, "end_line": 545, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setitem__", "qualified_name": "__setitem__", "args": ["self", "key", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 547, "end_line": 579, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_ipython_key_completions_", "qualified_name": "_ipython_key_completions_", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 581, "end_line": 582, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self", "order"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The Numpy documentation lies; `numpy.ndarray.copy` is not equivalent to\n`numpy.copy`.  Differences include that it re-views the copied array as\nself's ndarray subclass, as though it were taking a slice; this means\n``__array_finalize__`` is called and the copy shares all the array\nattributes (includi", "start_line": 584, "end_line": 597, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "columns", "qualified_name": "columns", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A user-visible accessor for the coldefs.", "start_line": 600, "end_