s": [], "docstring": "Given the column-specific time reference frame information, verify that\neach column-specific time coordinate attribute has a valid value.\nReturn True if the coordinate column is time, or else return False.\n\nParameters\n----------\nglobal_info : dict\n    Global time reference frame information.\ncolumn_", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 302, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_info_if_time_column", "qualified_name": "_get_info_if_time_column", "args": ["col", "global_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check if a column without corresponding time column keywords in the\nFITS header represents time or not. If yes, return the time column\ninformation needed for its conversion to Time.\nThis is only applicable to the special-case where a column has the\nname 'TIME' and a time unit.", "start_line": 305, "end_line": 334, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_global_time", "qualified_name": "_convert_global_time", "args": ["table", "global_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert the table metadata for time informational keywords\nto astropy Time.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntable : `~astropy.table.Table`\n    The table whose time metadata is to be converted.\nglobal_info : dict\n    Global time reference frame information.", "start_line": 337, "end_line": 356, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_time_key", "qualified_name": "_convert_time_key", "args": ["global_info", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a time metadata key to a Time object.\n\nParameters\n----------\nglobal_info : dict\n    Global time reference frame information.\nkey : str\n    Time key.\n\nReturns\n-------\nastropy.time.Time\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError\n    If key is not a valid global time keyword.", "start_line": 359, "end_line": 388, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_time_column", "qualified_name": "_convert_time_column", "args": ["col", "column_info"], "decorator