 "getdata", "qualified_name": "getdata", "args": ["filename"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the data from an HDU of a FITS file (and optionally the\nheader).\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    File to get data from.  If opened, mode must be one of the\n    following rb, rb+, or ab+.\n\next\n    The rest of the arguments are for HDU specification.\n    They are flexi", "start_line": 131, "end_line": 264, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "getval", "qualified_name": "getval", "args": ["filename", "keyword"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get a keyword's value from a header in a FITS file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    Name of the FITS file, or file object (if opened, mode must be\n    one of the following rb, rb+, or ab+).\n\nkeyword : str\n    Keyword name\n\next, extname, extver\n    The rest of the argumen", "start_line": 267, "end_line": 298, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "setval", "qualified_name": "setval", "args": ["filename", "keyword"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set a keyword's value from a header in a FITS file.\n\nIf the keyword already exists, it's value/comment will be updated.\nIf it does not exist, a new card will be created and it will be\nplaced before or after the specified location.  If no ``before`` or\n``after`` is specified, it will be appended at t", "start_line": 301, "end_line": 375, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "delval", "qualified_name": "delval", "args": ["filename", "keyword"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Delete all instances of keyword from a header in a FITS file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    Name of the FITS file, or file object If opened, mode must be update\n    (rb+).  An opened file object or `~gzip.GzipFile` object will be closed\n    upon return.\n\nkeyword : str,", "start_line": 378, "end_line": 410, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "writeto", "qualified_name": "writeto", "args": ["filename", "data", "header", "output_verify", "overwrite", "checksum"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new FITS file using the supplied data/header.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    File to write to.  If opened, must be opened in a writable binary\n    mode such as 'wb' or 'ab+'.\n\ndata : array or `~numpy.recarray` or `~astropy.io.fits.Group`\n    data to write to th", "start_line": 413, "end_line": 459, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "table_to_hdu", "qualified_name": "table_to_hdu", "args": ["table", "character_as_bytes"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert an `~astropy.table.Table` object to a FITS\n`~astropy.io.fits.BinTableHDU`.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntable : astropy.table.Table\n    The table to convert.\ncharacter_as_bytes : bool\n    Whether to return bytes for string columns when accessed from the HDU.\n    By default this is `False` and (uni", "start_line": 462, "end_line": 658, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "append", "qualified_name": "append", "args": ["filename", "data", "header", "checksum", "verify"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Append the header/data to FITS file if filename exists, create if not.\n\nIf only ``data`` is supplied, a minimal header is created.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    File to write to.  If opened, must be opened for update (rb+) unless it\n    is a new file, then it must be o", "start_line": 661, "end_line": 734, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update", "qualified_name": "update", "args": ["filename", "data"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the specified HDU with the input data/header.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    File to update.  If opened, mode must be update (rb+).  An opened file\n    object or `~gzip.GzipFile` object will be closed upon return.\n\ndata : array, `~astropy.table.Table`, or `~astro", "start_line": 737, "end_line": 792, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "info", "qualified_name": "info", "args": ["filename", "output"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Print the summary information on a FITS file.\n\nThis includes the name, type, length of header, data shape and type\nfor each HDU.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    FITS file to obtain info from.  If opened, mode must be one of\n    the following: rb, rb+, or ab+ (i.e. the fi", "start_line": 795, "end_line": 829, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "printdiff", "qualified_name": "printdiff", "args": ["inputa", "inputb"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compare two parts of a FITS file, including entire FITS files,\nFITS `HDUList` objects and FITS ``HDU`` objects.\n\nParameters\n----------\ninputa : str, `HDUList` object, or ``HDU`` object\n    The filename of a FITS file, `HDUList`, or ``HDU``\n    object to compare to ``inputb``.\n\ninputb : str, `HDUList", "start_line": 832, "end_line": 938, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "tabledump", "qualified_name": "tabledump", "args": ["filename", "datafile", "cdfile", "hfile", "ext", "overwrite"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Dump a table HDU to a file in ASCII format.  The table may be\ndumped in three separate files, one containing column definitions,\none containing header parameters, and one for table data.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilename : path-like or file-like\n    Input fits file.\n\ndatafile : path-like or file-like,", "start_line": 941, "end_line": 998, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "tableload", "qualified_name": "tableload", "args": ["datafile", "cdfile", "hfile"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a table from the input ASCII files.  The input is from up\nto three separate files, one containing column definitions, one\ncontaining header parameters, and one containing column data.  The\nheader parameters file is not required.  When the header\nparameters file is absent a minimal header is c", "start_line": 1005, "end_line": 1036, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_getext", "qualified_name": "_getext", "args": ["filename", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Open the input file, return the `HDUList` and the extension.\n\nThis supports several different styles of extension selection.  See the\n:func:`getdata()` documentation for the different possibilities.", "start_line": 1043, "end_line": 1115, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_makehdu", "qualified_name": "_makehdu", "args": ["data", "header"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1118, "end_line": 1133, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_stat_filename_or_fileobj", "qualified_name": "_stat_filename_or_fileobj", "args": ["filename"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1136, "end_line": 1151, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_file_mode", "qualified_name": "_get_file_mode", "args": ["filename", "default"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Allow file object to already be opened in any of the valid modes and\nand leave the file in the same state (opened or closed) as when\nthe function was called.", "start_line": 1154, "end_line": 1172, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Convenience functions for working with FITS files.\n\nConvenience functions\n=====================\n\nThe functions in this module provide shortcuts for some of the most basic\noperations on FITS files, such as reading and updating the header.  They are\nincluded directly in the 'astropy.io.fits' namespace so that they can be used\nlike::\n\n    astropy.io.fits.getheader(...)\n\nThese functions are primarily for convenience when working with FITS files in\nthe command-line interpreter.  If performing several operations on the same\nfile, such as in a script, it is better to *not* use these functions, as each\none must open and re-parse the file.  In such cases it is better to use\n:func:`astropy.io.fits.open` and work directly with the\n:class:`astropy.io.fits.HDUList` object and underlying HDU objects.\n\nSeveral of the convenience functions, such as `getheader` and `getdata` support\nspecial arguments for selecting which HDU to use when working with a\nmulti-extension FITS file.  There are a few supported argument formats for\nselecting the HDU.  See the documentation for `getdata` for an\nexplanation of all the different formats.\n\n.. warning::\n    All arguments to convenience functions other than the filename that are\n    *not* for selecting the HDU should be passed in as keyword\n    arguments.  This is to avoid ambiguity and conflicts with the\n    HDU arguments.  For example, to set NAXIS=1 on the Primary HDU:\n\n    Wrong::\n\n        astropy.io.fits.setval('myimage.fits', 'NAXIS', 1)\n\n    The above example will try to set the NAXIS value on the first extension\n    HDU to blank.  That is, the argument '1' is assumed to specify an\n    HDU.\n\n    Right::\n\n        astropy.io.fits.setval('myimage.fits', 'NAXIS', value=1)\n\n    This will set the NAXIS keyword to 1 on the primary HDU (the default).  To\n    specify the first extension HDU use::\n\n        astropy.io.fits.setval('myimage.fits', 'NAXIS', value=1, ext=1)\n\n    This complexity arises out of the attempt to simultaneously support\n    multiple argument formats that were used in past versions of PyFITS.\n    Unfortunately, it is not possible to support all formats without\n    introducing some ambiguity.  A future Astropy release may standardize\n    around a single format and officially deprecate the other formats.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/fits/diff.py", "file_hash": "f6323cf4e0ede5bcd1cddd42969de3e5e1fb70ffb5e3c5daebe8e219d2a74d2f", "imports": [{"module": "fnmatch", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "glob", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "io", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "operator", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "os", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "os.path", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "textwrap", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "collections", "names": ["defaultdict"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "inspect", "names": ["signature"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "itertools", "names": ["islice"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "astropy", "names": ["__version__"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.diff", "names": ["diff_values", "fixed_width_indent", "report_diff_values", "where_not_allclose"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "astropy.utils.misc", "names": ["NOT_OVERWRITING_MSG"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "card", "names": ["BLANK_CARD", "Card"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.hdulist", "names": ["HDUList", "fitsopen"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.table", "names": ["_TableLikeHDU"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "header", "names": ["Header"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "util", "names": ["path_like"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "report_diff_keyword_attr", "qualified_name": "report_diff_keyword_attr", "args": ["fileobj", "attr", "diffs", "keyword", "ind"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Write a diff between two header keyword values or comments to the specified\nfile-like object.", "start_line": 1557, "end_line": 1577, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The ``_BaseDiff`` class does not implement a ``_diff`` method and\nshould not be instantiated directly. Instead instantiate the\nappropriate subclass of ``_BaseDiff`` for the objects being compared\n(for example, use `HeaderDiff` to compare two `Header` objects.", "start_line": 73, "end_line": 87, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__bool__", "qualified_name": "__bool__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A ``_BaseDiff`` object acts as `True` in a boolean context if the two\nobjects compared are different.  Otherwise it acts as `False`.", "start_line": 89, "end_line": 94, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fromdiff", "qualified_name": "fromdiff", "args": ["cls", "other", "a", "b"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Returns a new Diff object of a specific subclass from an existing diff\nobject, passing on the values for any arguments they share in common\n(such as ignore_keywords).\n\nFor example::\n\n    >>> from astropy.io import fits\n    >>> hdul1, hdul2 = fits.HDUList(), fits.HDUList()\n    >>> headera, headerb = ", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 120, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "identical", "qualified_name": "identical", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "`True` if all the ``.diff_*`` attributes on this diff instance are\nempty, implying that no differences were found.\n\nAny subclass of ``_BaseDiff`` must have at least one ``.diff_*``\nattribute, which contains a non-empty value if and only if some\ndifference was found between the two objects being comp", "start_line": 123, "end_line": 134, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "report", "qualified_name": "report", "args": ["self", "fileobj", "indent", "overwrite"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generates a text report on the differences (if any) between two\nobjects, and either returns it as a string or writes it to a file-like\nobject.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfileobj : file-like, string, or None, optional\n    If `None`, this method returns the report as a string. Otherwise it\n    returns `No", "start_line": 136, "end_line": 186, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_writeln", "qualified_name": "_writeln", "args": ["self", "text"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 188, "end_line": 189, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 191, "end_line": 192, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 194, "end_line": 195, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "ignore_hdus", "ignore_keywords", "ignore_comments", "ignore_fields", "numdiffs", "rtol", "atol", "ignore_blanks", "ignore_blank_cards"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : str or `HDUList`\n    The filename of a FITS file on disk, or an `HDUList` object.\n\nb : str or `HDUList`\n    The filename of a FITS file on disk, or an `HDUList` object to\n    compare to the first file.\n\nignore_hdus : sequence, optional\n    HDU names to ignore when comparing", "start_line": 212, "end_line": 336, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 338, "end_line": 380, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 382, "end_line": 450, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "ignore_keywords", "ignore_comments", "ignore_fields", "numdiffs", "rtol", "atol", "ignore_blanks", "ignore_blank_cards"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object.\n\nb : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object to compare to the first HDU object.\n\nignore_keywords : sequence, optional\n    Header keywords to ignore when comparing two headers; the presence\n    of these keywords and their values are ignored.  Wildcard strings\n ", "start_line": 482, "end_line": 570, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 572, "end_line": 615, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 617, "end_line": 652, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "ignore_keywords", "ignore_comments", "rtol", "atol", "ignore_blanks", "ignore_blank_cards"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : `~astropy.io.fits.Header` or string or bytes\n    A header.\n\nb : `~astropy.io.fits.Header` or string or bytes\n    A header to compare to the first header.\n\nignore_keywords : sequence, optional\n    Header keywords to ignore when comparing two headers; the presence\n    of thes", "start_line": 698, "end_line": 822, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 827, "end_line": 927, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 929, "end_line": 970, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "numdiffs", "rtol", "atol"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object.\n\nb : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object to compare to the first HDU object.\n\nnumdiffs : int, optional\n    The number of pixel/table values to output when reporting HDU data\n    differences.  Though the count of differences is the same either\n    way, this ", "start_line": 1011, "end_line": 1060, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1062, "end_line": 1100, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1102, "end_line": 1136, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "numdiffs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object.\n\nb : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object to compare to the first HDU object.\n\nnumdiffs : int, optional\n    The number of pixel/table values to output when reporting HDU data\n    differences.  Though the count of differences is the same either\n    way, this ", "start_line": 1161, "end_line": 1181, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1183, "end_line": 1192, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1194, "end_line": 1224, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "a", "b", "ignore_fields", "numdiffs", "rtol", "atol"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\na : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object.\n\nb : BaseHDU\n    An HDU object to compare to the first HDU object.\n\nignore_fields : sequence, optional\n    The (case-insensitive) names of any table columns to ignore if any\n    table data is to be compared.\n\nnumdiffs : int, optional\n    The numbe", "start_line": 1275, "end_line": 1342, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_diff", "qualified_name": "_diff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1344, "end_line": 1488, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_report", "qualified_name": "_report", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1490, "end_line": 1554, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_header_values_comments", "qualified_name": "get_header_values_comments", "args": ["cards"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 836, "end_line": 845, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "_BaseDiff", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__bool__", "fromdiff", "identical", "report", "_writeln", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Base class for all FITS diff objects.\n\nWhen instantiating a FITS diff object, the first two arguments are always\nthe two objects to diff (two FITS files, two FITS headers, etc.).\nInstantiating a ``_BaseDiff`` also causes the diff itself to be executed.\nThe returned ``_BaseDiff`` instance has a numbe", "start_line": 58, "end_line": 195}, {"name": "FITSDiff", "bases": ["_BaseDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Diff two FITS files by filename, or two `HDUList` objects.\n\n`FITSDiff` objects have the following diff attributes:\n\n- ``diff_hdu_count``: If the FITS files being compared have different\n  numbers of HDUs, this contains a 2-tuple of the number of HDUs in each\n  file.\n\n- ``diff_hdus``: If any HDUs wit", "start_line": 198, "end_line": 450}, {"name": "HDUDiff", "bases": ["_BaseDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Diff two HDU objects, including their headers and their data (but only if\nboth HDUs contain the same type of data (image, table, or unknown).\n\n`HDUDiff` objects have the following diff attributes:\n\n- ``diff_extnames``: If the two HDUs have different EXTNAME values, this\n  contains a 2-tuple of the d", "start_line": 453, "end_line": 652}, {"name": "HeaderDiff", "bases": ["_BaseDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Diff two `Header` objects.\n\n`HeaderDiff` objects have the following diff attributes:\n\n- ``diff_keyword_count``: If the two headers contain a different number of\n  keywords, this contains a 2-tuple of the keyword count for each header.\n\n- ``diff_keywords``: If either header contains one or more keywo", "start_line": 655, "end_line": 970}, {"name": "ImageDataDiff", "bases": ["_BaseDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Diff two image data arrays (really any array from a PRIMARY HDU or an IMAGE\nextension HDU, though the data unit is assumed to be \"pixels\").\n\n`ImageDataDiff` objects have the following diff attributes:\n\n- ``diff_dimensions``: If the two arrays contain either a different number\n  of dimensions or diff", "start_line": 979, "end_line": 1136}, {"name": "RawDataDiff", "bases": ["ImageDataDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "`RawDataDiff` is just a special case of `ImageDataDiff` where the images\nare one-dimensional, and the data is treated as a 1-dimensional array of\nbytes instead of pixel values.  This is used to compare the data of two\nnon-standard extension HDUs that were not recognized as containing image or\ntable ", "start_line": 1139, "end_line": 1224}, {"name": "TableDataDiff", "bases": ["_BaseDiff"], "methods": ["__init__", "_diff", "_report"], "docstring": "Diff two table data arrays. It doesn't matter whether the data originally\ncame from a binary or ASCII table--the data should be passed in as a\nrecarray.\n\n`TableDataDiff` objects have the following diff attributes:\n\n- ``diff_column_count``: If the tables being compared have different\n  numbers of col", "start_line": 1227, "end_line": 1554}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Facilities for diffing two FITS files.  Includes objects for diffing entire\nFITS files, individual HDUs, FITS headers, or just FITS data.\n\nUsed to implement the fitsdiff program.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/fits/util.py", "file_hash": "7cc2c60800d837045fd0f950282b6bb419166e83ac67b524f47cfd5d84177a8b", "imports": [{"module": "gzip", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""},