o this\nobject.  This adds a weakref to the list of listeners that is\nremoved from the listeners list when the listener has no other\nreferences to it.", "start_line": 79, "end_line": 89, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_remove_listener", "qualified_name": "_remove_listener", "args": ["self", "listener"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Removes the specified listener from the listeners list.  This relies\non object identity (i.e. the ``is`` operator).", "start_line": 91, "end_line": 100, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_notify", "qualified_name": "_notify", "args": ["self", "notification"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Notify all listeners of some particular state change by calling their\n``_update_<notification>`` method with the given ``*args`` and\n``**kwargs``.\n\nThe notification does not by default include the object that actually\nchanged (``self``), but it certainly may if required.", "start_line": 102, "end_line": 125, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getstate__", "qualified_name": "__getstate__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Exclude listeners when saving the listener's state, since they may be\nephemeral.", "start_line": 127, "end_line": 142, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "wrapped", "qualified_name": "wrapped", "args": [], "decorators": ["wraps(func)"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 200, "end_line": 236, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pairwise", "qualified_name": "pairwise", "args": ["iterable"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the items of an iterable paired with its next item.\n\nEx: s -> (s0,s1), (s1,s2), (s2,s3), ....", "start_line": 245, "end_line": 255, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "maybe_fill", "qualified_name": "maybe_fill", "args": ["t"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 511, "end_line": 515, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args"