, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 871, "end_line": 875, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["name.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 878, "end_line": 888, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "match_header", "qualified_name": "match_header", "args": ["cls", "header"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 891, "end_line": 906, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_header_data", "qualified_name": "_update_header_data", "args": ["self", "image_header", "name", "compression_type", "tile_shape", "hcomp_scale", "hcomp_smooth", "quantize_level", "quantize_method", "dither_seed"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the table header (`_header`) to the compressed\nimage format and to match the input data (if any).  Create\nthe image header (`_image_header`) from the input image\nheader (if any) and ensure it matches the input\ndata. Create the initially-empty table data array to hold\nthe compressed data.\n\nThi", "start_line": 908, "end_line": 1519, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_scale_data", "qualified_name": "_scale_data", "args": ["self", "data"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1521, "end_line": 1543, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "data", "qualified_name": "data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "The decompressed data array.\n\nNote that accessing this will cause all the tiles to be loaded,\ndecompressed, and combined into a single data array. If you do\nnot need to access the whole array, consider instead using the\n:attr:`~astropy.io.fits.CompImageHDU.section` property.", "start_line": 1546, "end_line": 1566, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "data", "qualified_name": "data", "args": ["self