: 758, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "index_of", "qualified_name": "index_of", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the index of an HDU from the `HDUList`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nkey : int, str, tuple of (string, int) or BaseHDU\n    The key identifying the HDU.  If ``key`` is a tuple, it is of the\n    form ``(name, ver)`` where ``ver`` is an ``EXTVER`` value that must\n    match the HDU being searched for.\n\n  ", "start_line": 760, "end_line": 831, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_positive_index_of", "qualified_name": "_positive_index_of", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Same as index_of, but ensures always returning a positive index\nor zero.\n\n(Really this should be called non_negative_index_of but it felt\ntoo long.)\n\nThis means that if the key is a negative integer, we have to\nconvert it to the corresponding positive index.  This means\nknowing the length of the HDU", "start_line": 833, "end_line": 855, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "readall", "qualified_name": "readall", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Read data of all HDUs into memory.", "start_line": 857, "end_line": 862, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "flush", "qualified_name": "flush", "args": ["self", "output_verify", "verbose"], "decorators": ["ignore_sigint"], "docstring": "Force a write of the `HDUList` back to the file (for append and\nupdate modes only).\n\nParameters\n----------\noutput_verify : str\n    Output verification option.  Must be one of ``\"fix\"``,\n    ``\"silentfix\"``, ``\"ignore\"``, ``\"warn\"``, or\n    ``\"exception\"``.  May also be any combination of ``\"fix\"`` o", "start_line": 865, "end_line": 931, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_extend", "qualified_name": "update_extend", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make sure that if the primary header needs the keyword ``EXTEND`` that\nit has it 