_string_array_round_trip", "qualified_name": "test_string_array_round_trip", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/201", "start_line": 2162, "end_line": 2194, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_new_table_with_nd_column", "qualified_name": "test_new_table_with_nd_column", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for\nhttps://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/3", "start_line": 2196, "end_line": 2219, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_mismatched_tform_and_tdim", "qualified_name": "test_mismatched_tform_and_tdim", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Normally the product of the dimensions listed in a TDIMn keyword\nmust be less than or equal to the repeat count in the TFORMn keyword.\n\nThis tests that this works if less than (treating the trailing bytes\nas unspecified fill values per the FITS standard) and fails if the\ndimensions specified by TDIM", "start_line": 2221, "end_line": 2254, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_tdim_of_size_one", "qualified_name": "test_tdim_of_size_one", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/pull/3580", "start_line": 2256, "end_line": 2260, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing", "qualified_name": "test_slicing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/52", "start_line": 2262, "end_line": 2278, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_slicing", "qualified_name": "test_array_slicing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/55", "start_line": 2280, "end_line": 2294, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_broadcasting", "qualified_name": "test_array_broadcasting", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/pull/48", "start_line": 2296, "end_line": 2311, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_slicing_readonly", "qualified_name": "test_array_slicing_readonly", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Like test_array_slicing but with the file opened in 'readonly' mode.\nRegression test for a crash when slicing readonly memmap'd tables.", "start_line": 2313, "end_line": 2329, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_dump_load_round_trip", "qualified_name": "test_dump_load_round_trip", "args": ["self", "tablename"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.parametrize('tablename', ['table.fits', 'tb.fits'])"], "docstring": "A simple test of the dump/load methods; dump the data, column, and\nheader files and try to reload the table from them.", "start_line": 2332, "end_line": 2350, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_dump_load_array_colums", "qualified_name": "test_dump_load_array_colums", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/22\n\nEnsures that a table containing a multi-value array column can be\ndumped and loaded successfully.", "start_line": 2352, "end_line": 2371, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_load_guess_format", "qualified_name": "test_load_guess_format", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests loading a table dump with no supplied coldefs or header, so that\nthe table format has to be guessed at.  There is of course no exact\nscience to this; the table that's produced simply uses sensible guesses\nfor that format.  Ideally this should never have to be used.", "start_line": 2373, "end_line": 2412, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_attribute_field_shadowing", "qualified_name": "test_attribute_field_shadowing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/86\n\nNumpy recarray objects have a poorly-considered feature of allowing\nfield access by attribute lookup.  However, if a field name coincides\nwith an existing attribute/method of the array, the existing name takes\npresence (making the", "start_line": 2414, "end_line": 2437, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_from_bool_fields", "qualified_name": "test_table_from_bool_fields", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/113\n\nTests creating a table from a recarray containing numpy.bool columns.", "start_line": 2439, "end_line": 2455, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_from_bool_fields2", "qualified_name": "test_table_from_bool_fields2", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/215\n\nTests the case where a multi-field ndarray (not a recarray) containing\na bool field is used to initialize a `BinTableHDU`.", "start_line": 2457, "end_line": 2467, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_bool_column_update", "qualified_name": "test_bool_column_update", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/139", "start_line": 2469, "end_line": 2483, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_missing_tnull", "qualified_name": "test_missing_tnull", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/197", "start_line": 2485, "end_line": 2514, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_blank_field_zero", "qualified_name": "test_blank_field_zero", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/5134\n\nBlank values in numerical columns of ASCII tables should be replaced\nwith zeros, so they can be loaded into numpy arrays.\n\nWhen a TNULL value is set and there are blank fields not equal to that\nvalue, they should be replaced with ze", "start_line": 2516, "end_line": 2569, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_column_array_type_mismatch", "qualified_name": "test_column_array_type_mismatch", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/218", "start_line": 2571, "end_line": 2576, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_none", "qualified_name": "test_table_none", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test\nfor https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/27", "start_line": 2578, "end_line": 2595, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_unncessary_table_load", "qualified_name": "test_unncessary_table_load", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test unnecessary parsing and processing of FITS tables when writing\ndirectly from one FITS file to a new file without first reading the\ndata for user manipulation.\n\nIn other words, it should be possible to do a direct copy of the raw\ndata without unnecessary processing of the data.", "start_line": 2597, "end_line": 2616, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_from_columns_of_other_table", "qualified_name": "test_table_from_columns_of_other_table", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests a rare corner case where the columns of an existing table\nare used to create a new table with the new_table function.  In this\nspecific case, however, the existing table's data has not been read\nyet, so new_table has to get at it through the Delayed proxy.\n\nNote: Although this previously teste", "start_line": 2618, "end_line": 2645, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_bintable_to_asciitable", "qualified_name": "test_bintable_to_asciitable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests initializing a TableHDU with the data from a BinTableHDU.", "start_line": 2647, "end_line": 2666, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_pickle", "qualified_name": "test_pickle", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/1597\n\nTests for pickling FITS_rec objects", "start_line": 2668, "end_line": 2703, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_zero_length_table", "qualified_name": "test_zero_length_table", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2705, "end_line": 2713, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_dim_column_byte_order_mismatch", "qualified_name": "test_dim_column_byte_order_mismatch", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "When creating a table column with non-trivial TDIMn, and\nbig-endian array data read from an existing FITS file, the data\nshould not be unnecessarily byteswapped.\n\nRegression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/3561", "start_line": 2715, "end_line": 2730, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_fits_rec_from_existing", "qualified_name": "test_fits_rec_from_existing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests creating a `FITS_rec` object with `FITS_rec.from_columns`\nfrom an existing `FITS_rec` object read from a FITS file.\n\nThis ensures that the per-column arrays are updated properly.\n\nRegression test for https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/99", "start_line": 2732, "end_line": 2762, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_update_string_column_inplace", "qualified_name": "test_update_string_column_inplace", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/4452\n\nEnsure that changes to values in a string column are saved when\na file is opened in ``mode='update'``.", "start_line": 2764, "end_line": 2805, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_reference_leak", "qualif