y.\n\nLike `numpy.ndarray.view`, but always returning a masked array subclass.", "start_line": 556, "end_line": 579, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_finalize__", "qualified_name": "__array_finalize__", "args": ["self", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 581, "end_line": 598, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The shape of the data and the mask.\n\nUsually used to get the current shape of an array, but may also be\nused to reshape the array in-place by assigning a tuple of array\ndimensions to it.  As with `numpy.reshape`, one of the new shape\ndimensions can be -1, in which case its value is inferred from the", "start_line": 601, "end_line": 617, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self", "shape"], "decorators": ["shape.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 620, "end_line": 641, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__eq__", "qualified_name": "__eq__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 650, "end_line": 660, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__ne__", "qualified_name": "__ne__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 662, "end_line": 672, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_combine_masks", "qualified_name": "_combine_masks", "args": ["self", "masks", "out", "where", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Combine masks, possibly storing it in some output.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmasks : tuple of array of bool or None\n    Input masks.  Any that are `None` or `False` are ignored.\n    Should broadcast to each other.\nout : output mask array, optional\n    Possible output array to hold the result.\nwhere : a", "start_line": 674, "end_line": 703, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_ufunc__", "qualified_name": 